hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","1798 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father from al-Hadrami from al-Qasim from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: There was a woman in Jiyad called Umm Mahzul, and she used to fornicate, and she stipulated for whoever married her that she would suffice him maintenance. A man sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to marry her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: (The fornicator does not marry except a fornicatress) the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mu'tamir."
"1802","1799 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dates and raisins being mixed together. No one narrated this hadith from Thuwayr except Isra'il."
"1803","1800 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri who said: I and Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar went out until we came to Hims. We came to Wahshi ibn Harb and he narrated to us, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and testified the testimony of truth. He said: O Wahshi, sit and tell me how you killed Hamzah? I told him, and he said: Hide your face from me, so I do not see you. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl except Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Majishun."
"1804","1801 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Samiri narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began the takbir in prayer, would raise his hands when he said the takbir until he placed them level with his shoulders, then when he said takbir and bowed he would do likewise, then when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he would do likewise, and say: Our Lord, to You is praise, and he would not do that when he prostrated nor when he rose from prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Uways except Ibrahim."
"1805","1802 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Amr ibn Jud'an: When you buy sandals, buy new ones, and when you buy a garment, buy a new one. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Abu Umayyah; al-Fayd alone narrated it."
"1806","1803 - Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Hashim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Matar al-Shaybani narrated to us from Ma'mar ibn Rashid from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who corrupts a woman against her husband, and he is not of us who corrupts a slave against his master. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Tawus except Ma'mar, nor from Ma'mar except Uthman; Ali alone narrated it."
"1807","1804 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from his father Ka'b ibn Malik that he narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Aws ibn al-Hadathan, and he announced: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking. This hadith is not narrated from Ka'b ibn Malik except with this chain; Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"1808","1805 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a mat. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Sharik; Muhammad ibn Hassan alone narrated it."
"1809","1806 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Rib'i from Hudhayfah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Fudayl alone narrated it."
"1810","1807 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Waqid ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard Nafi' narrate from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine. No one narrated this hadith from Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Umar except Shu'bah."
"1811","1808 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sakan Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Sakan al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Harith from Darraj from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every qunut in the Qur'an means obedience. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Rishdin."
"1812","1809 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah narrated to us from al-Suddi from Abd Khayr who said: We were in the mosque and Ali came out to us at the end of the night and said: Where is the one asking about Witr? We gathered to him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Witr at the beginning of the night, then performed Witr in its middle, then performed Witr at this hour, and he passed away while performing Witr at this hour. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Abu Shaybah."
"1813","1810 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra' narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding al-Hasan ibn Ali: This son of mine is a leader, and Allah will reconcile through him between two great parties of Muslims. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abd al-Rahman and Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"1814","1811 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of the people of Hell I have not yet seen: women clothed yet naked, deviating and causing deviation, upon their heads like the humps of Bukht camels, and people with whips like the tails of cattle. They will not enter Paradise nor find its scent. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Zuhayr."
"1815","1812 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ka'b ibn Ujrah al-Ansari that he narrated to him that he had entered ihram in Dhu al-Qa'dah for Hajj, and his head became lousy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon him while he was kindling fire under a pot of his, and said to him: Do the vermin of your head harm you? He said: Yes. He said: Shave, and offer a sacrificial animal. I said: I cannot find a sacrificial animal. He said: Then feed six poor persons. He said: I cannot. He said: Then fast three days. He said: I shaved and fasted three days. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"1816","1813 - And with the same chain: from Abu al-Zubayr from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from al-Ta'if until when he was at Batn Nakhlah the people crowded upon him and pressed him. He passed by a lote tree, and it caught his cloak, so his cloak remained. He turned to us with his face as if it were a piece of the moon, and as if his neck were strings of gold, and said: O people, enable me to get my cloak. Do you fear miserliness from me? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I had red camels like the trees of Awtas I would distribute them among you. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim."
"1817","1814 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a stabber, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Alqamah except Isra'il; Muhammad ibn Sabiq alone narrated it."
"1818","1815 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah from Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah from his father who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smeared with khaluq perfume, wearing patched garments, having entered ihram for Umrah, and said: How do you command me, O Messenger of Allah, regarding my Umrah? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: (And complete Hajj and Umrah for Allah). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the one asking about Umrah? He said: I am. He said: Cast off your clothes, wash, clean yourself as much as you can, and whatever you would do in your Hajj, do it in your Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim. Abu al-Zubayr did not place anyone between Ata' and Safwan, and Mujahid narrated it from Ata' from Safwan ibn Ya'la from his father."
"1819","1816 - And with the same chain: from Abu al-Zubayr from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came at the conquest, the conquest of Makkah, he stayed at the upper part of Makkah and prayed eight rak'ahs. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer? He said: The Duha prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim."
"1820","1817 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ubayd ibn Umayr from A'ishah who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from this, and she pointed to a brass vessel placed like a sa'; we both drew from it together, and I would pour over my head three times with my hands, without undoing my hair. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ayyub, Rawh ibn al-Qasim, and Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"1821","1818 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us from Ibrahim from Abu al-Zubayr from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah from Umm Kurz who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The aqiqah for the boy is two equivalent sheep, and for the girl one sheep."
"1822","1819 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Sulayman al-Jawzajani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Abu Hanifah from Bilal from Wahb ibn Kaysan from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud and the takbir as he taught us a surah of the Qur'an. No one narrated this hadith from Wahb except Bilal; Abu Hanifah alone narrated it."
"1823","1820 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. I said: Did he marry her in Makkah? He said: No, but he married her on part of the road. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim."
"1824","1821 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abdullah ibn Rafi', freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I tighten the braids of my head; should I undo them when janabah befalls me? He said: It suffices you to scoop with your hand three scoops of water and pour it upon your head, then wash the rest of your body, and then you are purified. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Muhammad. Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Sufyan al-Thawri, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, Rawh ibn al-Qasim, and others narrated it from Ayyub ibn Musa."
"1825","1822 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Aziz narrate from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and there is nothing before him screening him, and one of you wants to pass before him, let him prevent him; if he refuses, let him fight him. Abu Abd al-Aziz from whom Shu'bah narrates this hadith is Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi."
"1826","1823 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us from Abd al-A'la, he said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral, and he said takbir five times. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla walked to him, took his hand, and said: Did you forget? He said: No, but I prayed behind my close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said takbir five times. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-A'la except Isra'il."
"1827","1824 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us from Abu Sinan from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir from Mujahid from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sleep except upon Witr. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Qays except Abu Sinan, nor from Abu Sinan except Mihran; Muhammad ibn Humayd alone narrated it."
"1828","1825 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us from Thabit ibn Ajlan from Sulaym ibn Amir who said: I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq dye with henna and katam, while Umar did not dye, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grows a white hair in the way of Allah, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Muhammad."
"1829","1826 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Qarm from Harun ibn Sa'd from Atiyyah al-Awfi who said: I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Who are the People of the House from whom Allah removed impurity and purified thoroughly? He counted them on his hand, five: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn. Abu Sa'id said: In the house of Umm Salamah this verse was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Harun except Sulayman; al-Ahwas alone narrated it."
"1830","1827 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib al-Ta'ifi narrated to us from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Sabrah from al-Qasim ibn Habib from Abd al-Malik ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of my ummah for whom I intercede are the people of Madinah, then the people of Makkah, then the people of al-Ta'if. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far except with this chain; Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib alone narrated it."
"1831","1828 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us from Fudayl ibn Marzuq from Atiyyah from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever wakes sound in his body, safe in his dwelling, having his day's provision, it is as if the world has been gathered for him. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Ali; Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"1832","1829 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanbah narrated to us from Raqabah ibn Masqalah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Khosrow perishes there will be no Khosrow after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will be spent in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1833","1830 - And with the same chain: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will never enter Hell who prayed before the rising of the sun and before its setting. No one narrated these two hadiths from Raqabah except Ibrahim."
"1834","1831 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Sayf Abu Dawud al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bazi' narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Mis'ar ibn Kidam from Asim from Zirr from Safwan ibn Assal who said: When we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would not remove our khuffs for three days and their nights, neither for stool, nor urine, nor sleep, except for janabah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Sa'id."
"1835","1832 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from A'ishah that she wanted to give charity of spoiled meat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Would you give as charity what you would not eat. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Khalid."
"1836","1833 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Marzuq al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seeking out the faults of women. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri except al-Hasan."
"1837","1834 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Zard al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Abi Basir from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Fajr prayer and said: Did so-and-so attend? They said: No. He said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: These two prayers are the heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites, and if they knew what is in them they would come to them even crawling. The front row is like the row of the angels; if you knew its virtue you would hasten to it. The prayer of a man with (another) man is purer than his prayer alone, and his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with (one) man, and the more numerous, the more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except Sa'id; Muhammad ibn Sufyan alone narrated it."
"1838","1835 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ubaydullah al-Darisi narrated to us, he said: Hazim ibn Bakr narrated to us from Yazid ibn Iyad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever invokes blessings upon me in a book, the angels continue to seek forgiveness for him as long as my name remains in that book. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1839","1836 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Dawud ibn Subayh al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: (And when his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it crumble), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed with the little finger; from its light He made it crumble. No one narrates this hadith from Shu'bah except Dawud."
"1840","1837 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Nuh narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ummah except part of it is in Paradise and part of it is in Hell, except my ummah, for it is in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Ishaq, nor from Ishaq except Muhammad; Ahmad alone narrated it."
"1841","1838 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from his father from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from A'ishah who said: When it was the day of Umm Habibah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), someone knocked at the door. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: See who this is. They said: Mu'awiyah. He said: Admit him. He entered with a pen on his ear with which he writes. He said: What is this pen on your ear, O Mu'awiyah? He said: A pen I prepared for Allah and His Messenger. He said: May Allah reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. By Allah, I employed you as a scribe only by revelation from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and I do nothing small or great except by revelation from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. How will you be when Allah clothes you a shirt? Meaning: the caliphate. Umm Habibah stood and sat before him and said: O Messenger of Allah, will Allah really clothe my brother a shirt? He said: Yes, but in it are flaws and flaws and flaws. She said: O Messenger of Allah, then supplicate for him. He said: O Allah, guide him with guidance, keep him away from destruction, and forgive him in the Hereafter and the first life. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abdullah ibn Yahya; al-Sari alone narrated it."
"1842","1839 - Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Mada'ini, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from A'ishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Musa said: O Lord, inform me of the most honored of Your creation to You. He said: The one who hastens to My desire as the eagle hastens to its desire, and the one devoted to My righteous servants as the child is devoted to people, and the one who becomes angry when My prohibitions are violated like the anger of the leopard for itself, for when the leopard becomes angry it does not care whether people are few or many. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abdullah; al-Musayyibi alone narrated it."
"1843","1840 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh narrated to us from Abu Ma'shar from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the expedition of Tabuk, and went to relieve himself, so I poured upon him; he washed his face three times and his hands three times, wiped his head, then wiped upon his khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Abu Ma'shar, nor from Abu Ma'shar except Abdullah; al-Musayyibi alone narrated it."
"1844","1841 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari from Anas ibn Malik who said: A sinking eastward was mentioned in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some people said: O Messenger of Allah, will a land in which there are Muslims be sunk? He said: Yes, when most of its people are wicked. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Anas; al-Musayyibi alone narrated it."
"1845","1842 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to me from al-Layth ibn Sa'd from Bakr ibn Sawadah from Ata' ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Two men went out on a journey, prayer came while they had no water, so they performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water; one of them repeated the prayer and the other did not. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not repeat: You hit the Sunnah, and your prayer sufficed you. And he said to the one who performed ablution and repeated: For you is the reward twice. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth with a connected chain except Abdullah; al-Musayyibi alone narrated it."
"1846","1843 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi' al-Uqayli from Salim from Ibn Umar regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: (As a niche), he said: The cavity of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the glass: his heart. And the lamp: the light in his heart, kindled from a blessed tree; the tree is Ibrahim, neither eastern nor western: neither Jewish nor Christian. Then he recited: (Ibrahim was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was upright, a Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists). No one narrated this hadith from Salim except al-Wazi'; Ali alone narrated it."
"1847","1844 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Azdi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Mansur from Talhah ibn Musarrif from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to admit a woman to her husband who had received nothing of her dowry. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur with a connected chain except Sharik."
"1848","1845 - Ahmad ibn Zanjawayh al-Qattan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar, judge of Aleppo, narrated to us from al-Fadl ibn Isa al-Raqashi from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created the intellect, He said to it: Stand, so it stood. Then He said to it: Turn back, so it turned back. Then He said to it: Sit, so it sat. He said: By My might, I have not created anything better than you, nor nobler than you, nor more excellent than you, nor more beautiful. By you I take, and by you I give, and by you I am known, and by you I punish; by you is reward, and upon you is punishment."
"1849","1846 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Musa al-Tarsusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reviles any of my companions, upon him is the curse of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Muhammad."
"1850","1847 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Nafi' from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks in a vessel of silver only gargles fire in his belly. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Razzaq."
"1851","1848 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Awf al-A'rabi from Abu Raja' al-Utaridi from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while hating three tribes: Thaqif, Banu Hanifah, and Banu Umayyah. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Ja'far, nor from Ja'far except Abd al-Razzaq; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone narrated it."
"1852","1849 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sneezed, would cover his face. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri except Abd al-Razzaq; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone narrated it."
"1853","1850 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Ta'i al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Nafi' ibn Abi Nu'aym and Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you touches his private part with his hand with no barrier between, ablution has become obligatory upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Abd al-Rahman."
"1854","1851 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Birti narrated to us in Baghdad, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us from Abu Khaldah from Maymun al-Kurdi from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not once nor twice nor three times until he reached ten times: Any man who marries a woman for a small or large dowry with no intention in himself to fulfill her right to her, deceiving her, then dies without fulfilling her right, will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer. And any man who takes a loan with no intention to fulfill its owner's right, deceiving him until he takes his wealth, then dies without fulfilling it, will meet Allah as a thief. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Maymun al-Kurdi except with this chain; Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, alone narrated it."
"1855","1852 - Ahmad ibn Abi Awf al-Mu'addal narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us from Abu Khalid al-Walibi from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What I fear most for my ummah is seeking rain by the stars, the injustice of the ruler, and denial of divine decree. No one narrated this hadith from Fitr except Muhammad, and it is not narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except with this chain."
"1856","1853 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Abu Salamah Sa'id ibn Yazid from Abu Nadrah al-Mundhir ibn Malik al-Abdi from Anas ibn Malik who said: Umm Sulaym sent me with fresh ripe dates to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a tray at the first ripening of the palm fruit. He said: I entered upon him and placed it before him, and he took some of it. Then he took my hand and we went out. He had recently married Zaynab bint Jahsh. He passed by some of his wives with men talking with them, and they congratulated him and the people congratulated him, saying: Praise be to Allah who has delighted your eye, O Messenger of Allah. He went on until he came to A'ishah, and there were two men with her, and he disliked that; when he disliked something it was known in his face. I came to Umm Sulaym and informed her. Abu Talhah said: If what your son says is true, something will happen. In the evening the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and ascended the minbar, and recited this verse: (O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permitted to you) the whole verse. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Nadrah except Abu Salamah; Khalid alone narrated it."
"1857","1854 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to me from Jabir ibn Yazid from Mujahid from Abu Rayhanah who said: People mentioned pride before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Prophet of Allah, I love beauty even in the strap of my whip and the lace of my sandal; do you fear anything in that for me? He said: No. We said: Then what is pride? He said: Pride is that which rejects the truth and despises people. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Abu Yazid."
"1858","1855 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Sa'ri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah informed him from her mother Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard disputants at his door, so he went out to them and said: O Allah, I am only a human; disputants come to me, and perhaps some of them are more eloquent in their argument than others, so I judge for him thinking him truthful. Whatever I decree for him of a Muslim's right is only a piece of Fire, so let him take it or leave it."
"1859","1856 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Khalid al-Madani narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is weak, patching; blessed is he who perishes upon his patching. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Sa'id; Ya'qub alone narrated it. Abu al-Qasim said: The interpretation of his saying (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): weak, patching, means: sinful, repentant."
"1860","1857 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn al-Azhar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from al-A'mash from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, a mosque like the nesting place of a sandgrouse, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will build for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Sharik; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1861","1858 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Isa al-Wasiti Sam'an narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala' al-Basri narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding wiping upon the khuffs: three days for the traveler, and for the resident a day until the night."
"1862","1859 - And with the same chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first thing the servant will be judged by on the Day of Resurrection is prayer; if it is sound, the rest of his deeds will be sound for him, and if it is corrupt, the rest of his deeds will be corrupt."
"1863","1860 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala' al-Basri from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated on Thursday evening, saying: O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar ibn al-Khattab or Amr ibn Hisham. On Friday morning Umar became Muslim. These three hadiths are not narrated from Anas except with this chain; al-Qasim alone narrated them."
"1864","1861 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Amir ibn Mus'ab al-Zuhri from A'ishah who said: A woman was divorced at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she remained twenty nights, then delivered her load. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Prosper with your matter, meaning: marry. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Sharik; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1865","1862 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr al-Hamdani informed us from Isma'il al-Suddi from Abu al-Minhal from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for my ummah four traits; He gave me three and withheld one. I asked Him that my ummah not disbelieve in a single bargain, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to set over them an enemy from others besides them, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to punish them as He punished the nations before them, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to place their strife among them, and He withheld it from me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Asbat; al-Anqazi alone narrated it."
"1866","1863 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them, and theirs is a painful punishment: a man who swore upon merchandise that he was offered more than he was offered, while lying; a man who swore a false oath after Asr to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man; and a man who withheld surplus water, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: Today I withhold from you My bounty as you withheld the surplus of what... No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Sa'id."
"1867","1864 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ajlan and Amr ibn Dinar from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the expedition of Hunayn, at part of the road the people asked him and crowded him; his she-camel became frightened, and a samurah tree caught his cloak. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return my cloak to me. Do you fear miserliness from me? By Allah, if Allah bestowed upon you camels like the number of the samur trees of Tihamah I would distribute them among you, then you would not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar. When it came to the division of the fifth, a man stood asking him to make lawful a needle or thread. He said: Return the needle and the thread, for misappropriation is shame, fire, and disgrace upon its people on the Day of Resurrection. Then he lifted a hair from the top of a camel's hump and said: I have of what Allah bestowed upon you not even like this except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ibn Uyaynah; al-Makhzumi alone narrated it."
"1868","1865 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Qays al-Ansari narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father from his grandfather from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What I fear most for my ummah after me: a man who interprets the Qur'an, placing it on other than its places, and a man who sees himself more deserving of this affair than others."
"1869","1866 - And with the same chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When (Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan) was revealed, Ibn al-Dahdah said: Does our Lord seek a loan from our wealth, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: I have two gardens, one in the highland and the other in the lowland, and I have lent the better of them to my Lord. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is for the orphan with you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a date cluster for Ibn al-Dahdah in Paradise hanging low. These two hadiths are not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ahmad alone narrated them."
"1870","1867 - Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Askari narrated to us in Surra man ra'a, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Khalid narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is weak, patching; blessed is he who perishes upon his patching. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Sa'id; Ya'qub alone narrated it."
"1871","1868 - Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Surayj al-Qadi Abu al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Sawrah ibn al-Hakam al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us from al-Sha'bi from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are given their reward twice: a man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and believed in him; a man who had a slave girl, freed her and married her; and a slave who feared Allah and obeyed his masters. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Habib except Sawrah."
"1872","1869 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Buhlul al-Anbari al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Salih from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lift the stick from your family, and frighten them regarding Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar except al-Hasan, nor from al-Hasan except Suwayd; Ishaq ibn al-Buhlul alone narrated it."
"1873","1870 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Khanzi al-Mu'adhdhin al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yazid ibn Iyad from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Ata' ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mulamasah."
"1874","1871 - And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. No one narrated these two hadiths from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Yazid ibn Iyad; Ibn Wahb alone narrated them."
"1875","1872 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Hafs al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cry of the newborn when born is a prick of Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Awanah except Shayban."
"1876","1873 - Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Rassasi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salamah from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with a black turban upon his head. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except al-Rassasi; Harmalah ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"1877","1874 - Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, he said: Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me from Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Nafi' from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will grasp the earth with His hand and the heavens with His right, then say: I am the King."
"1878","1875 - And from Ibn Shihab from Nafi' from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The parable of the companion of the Qur'an when he binds himself upon it and stands with it in his night is like tied camels: when its owner ties it he holds it, and when he releases it it escapes."
"1879","1876 - And from Ibn Shihab from Nafi' from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fever is from the blast of Hell, so cool it with water. And Ibn Umar used to say: O Allah, remove impurity from us. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, nor from Uqayl except Haywah, nor from Haywah except Idris ibn Yahya; Harmalah alone narrated them."
"1880","1877 - Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed me from Sulayman ibn Mihran al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Alqamah ibn Qays from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five rak'ahs, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Jarir except Ibn Wahb."
"1881","1878 - Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us from Jarir ibn Hazim from Qatadah from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Jarir; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"1882","1879 - Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, he said: Hammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil, who was our neighbor, narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My ummah is a merciful nation, repented upon; it enters its graves with its sins and exits its graves with no sins upon it; its sins are purged from it by the seeking of forgiveness of the believers for it. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad ibn Ziyad; Harmalah alone narrated it."
"1883","1880 - Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me from al-Zuhri from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When supper is served and prayer is called, begin with supper, and do not hasten from your supper. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibn Wahb and Rawh ibn Ubadah."
"1884","1881 - Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to me, he said: Ibn Wahb and Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafi'i narrated to us, they said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls. Al-Shafi'i used to add in his hadith: Ibn Umm Maktum would not call until it was said to him: Morning, morning. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibn Wahb and al-Shafi'i."
"1885","1882 - Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj from Salim from his father from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Consult women regarding themselves. No one narrated this hadith except Ibn Wahb."
"1886","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mujabbar informed me, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When it is his seventh day, shed blood on his behalf, remove harm from him, and name him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mujabbar except Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1887","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: We, the company of the Prophets, were commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, to delay our sahur, and to place our right hands over our left hands in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Ibn Wahb; Harmalah ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it."
"1888","Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to me, he said: A short man from the people of Egypt in the gathering of Al-Zuhri, called Amr ibn al-Harith, narrated to me, from Abu Hubayrah, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you see the servant granted detachment from this world and fewness of speech, draw close to him, for he casts forth wisdom."
"1889","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Al-Sakan ibn Abi Karimah, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: O Allah, dictate my proof to me, for the disbeliever is dictated his proof; rather let him say: O Allah, grant the proof of faith at death. No one narrated this hadith from Al-Zuhri except Al-Sakan ibn Abi Karimah, nor from Al-Sakan except Ibn Lahiah; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1890","Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Masud Al-Madi ibn Muhammad al-Ghafiqi informed me, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Al-Hasan, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the most wretched of the wretched? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He upon whom are combined the poverty of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Al-Madi ibn Muhammad; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1891","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Muhammad ibn Uqayl, from Al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is visited at four traits: when he sleeps alone, when he sleeps lying on his back, when he sleeps in a saffron-dyed sheet, and when he bathes in open ground; so whoever can avoid bathing in open ground, and if he must do it, let him draw a line. This hadith is not narrated from Al-Zuhri except with this chain; Abd al-Majid was alone in narrating it."
"1892","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen. A man said: And our east, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen. The man said: And our east, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen; indeed from there rises the horn of Satan, and therein are nine-tenths of disbelief, and therein is the incurable disease. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata except Said ibn Abi Ayyub; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1893","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Tamim al-Muradi narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If I had this world and all that is in it for this verse: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed Allah forgives all sins; indeed He is the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful. A man said to him: And whoever associates partners? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except whoever associates partners."
"1894","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: My grandfather narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash al-Qitbani narrated to me, from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams, one on behalf of himself and his household, and the other on behalf of himself and whoever among his ummah did not sacrifice."
"1895","Ahmad ibn Tahir narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Rabi al-Nawfali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Rishdin narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, seizes the scholars by seizure, and seizes knowledge along with them, so young newcomers grow up, some of them mounting upon others like the mounting of camels upon camels, and the old man among them is treated as weak. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Rishdin; Al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin was alone in narrating it."
"1896","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of al-araya by their estimated measure. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Anbasah; Ahmad ibn Salih was alone in narrating it."
"1897","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Hudaydah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, from his brother Al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah, from his father Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There follows a man among good deeds on the Day of Resurrection like mountains, so he says: From where is this? So it is said: By your child's seeking forgiveness for you. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Atiyyah except Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah."
"1898","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah al-Nakhai, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in a single garment. No one narrated this hadith from Al-Layth except Ibn Wahb; Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb was alone in narrating it."
"1899","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created the heaven? So he says: Allah. Then he says: Who created the earth? So he says: Allah. Then he says: Who created Allah? So when one of you finds that, let him say: I believe in Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, except Malik, nor from Malik except Ibn Abi Uways; Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh was alone in narrating it. And the people narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"1900","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Musa ibn Yaqub, nor from Musa except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ahmad ibn Salih was alone in narrating it."
"1901","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Two men disputed over a palm tree, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut a stalk from its stalks, found its measure to be five cubits, and made that its sanctuary. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Yahya except Al-Darawardi."
"1902","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Said ibn Kathir ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi informed me, from his father, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: Grapes from Taif were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave me a cluster and said: Take it to your mother; but I ate it on the way. So he said: What happened to the cluster? I said: I ate it. So he named me Ghudar. And al-Numan used to say upon his minbar: Indeed the whole calamity is to do evil deeds in evil oaths. This hadith is not narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq was alone in narrating it."
"1903","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I read to Abd Allah ibn Nafi, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the believer falls ill, that purifies him just as the bellows purifies the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ibn Abi Dhib; Abd Allah ibn Nafi was alone in narrating it."
"1904","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me in green garments hung with pearls. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Al-Husayn ibn Waqid; Zayd ibn al-Hubab was alone in narrating it."
"1905","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting: Does he think that his wealth will make him immortal. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Al-Dhimari."
"1906","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Rabiah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning in a state of janabah from intercourse, not from a wet dream. No one narrated this hadith from Rabiah except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ibn Abi Uways was alone in narrating it, from his brother."
"1907","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Thabit ibn Mujammi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, that he wiped over the two khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Ismail ibn Thabit, nor from Ismail except Yahya al-Jari; Ahmad ibn Salih was alone in narrating it."
"1908","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from the daughter of Nubayt, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it, so when you come to it, eat from its trees, even from its thorny trees. This hadith was not narrated from Zaynab bint Nubayt except with this chain; Al-Darawardi was alone in narrating it."
"1909","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to travel with the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing the enemy would get hold of it."
"1910","And from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed when one of you dies, his seat is presented to him morning and evening; if he is among the people of Paradise or among the people of Hell, it is said: This is your seat until Allah resurrects you from it."
"1911","And from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd narrated to me, from Hafsah or Aishah or both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over her husband. No one narrated these hadiths from Abd Allah ibn Dinar except Salih ibn Qudamah."
"1912","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Burullusi narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Malik ibn Anas, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let no one milk anyone's livestock without his permission; would one of you like his storeroom to be approached, his chest broken, and his food taken away? For the udders of their cattle store their foods for them, so let no one milk anyone's livestock except with his permission. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had except Haywah ibn Shurayh and Bakr ibn Mudar; Abd Allah ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it from Haywah, and from Bakr ibn Mudar, his son Ishaq ibn Bakr."
"1913","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd al-Faraidi al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The cutting is for a quarter of a dinar and upward."
"1914","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd al-Faraidi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell never combine in the belly of a Muslim man. No one narrated these two hadiths from Malik except Al-Hunayni."
"1915","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We acquired nothing of this world of yours except your women. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in narrating it."
"1916","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my maternal uncle: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: I used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when it descended upon him he was seized by severe distress and sweated profusely like pearls, then it was lifted from him; so I would enter upon him with a piece of shoulder blade or a fragment, and I would write while he dictated to me; I would not finish until my leg almost broke from the weight of the Quran, until I would say: I will never walk on my leg again; then when I finished, he said: Read it, so I would read it, and if there was any omission he would correct it, then I would go out with it to the people."
"1917","And from Ibn Shihab, that Salim ibn Abd Allah informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched."
"1918","And from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad al-Muqad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a matter to hold fast to. So he said: Keep control over this for yourself, and he pointed to his tongue."
"1919","From Ibn Shihab, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar narrated to him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drinker while he was at Khaybar, so he threw dust in his face, then he ordered his companions and they beat him with their sandals and with what was in their hands, until he said to them: Be gentle, so they were gentle; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while that was his sunnah; then Abu Bakr flogged forty for wine, then Umar flogged forty at the beginning of his rule, then flogged eighty at the end of his caliphate, then Uthman flogged the hadd forty, then Muawiyah flogged the hadd forty."
"1920","And from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The keys of the unseen are five, then he recited this verse: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs; and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"1921","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my maternal uncle: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, that his father wrote to him: Meet Subayah al-Aslamiyyah and ask her how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled for her. He said: So Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan informed me that Subayah al-Aslamiyyah informed him that her husband Sad ibn Khawlah died in Makkah along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the Farewell Hajj while she was pregnant, and she did not remain after him but a short while until she gave birth; then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak ibn al-Sabbaq of Banu Abd al-Dar proposed to her, but she refused to marry him, so he said: You are not lawful until you complete the longer of the two terms. So she sought a fatwa from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he permitted her to marry. No one narrated this hadith from Uqayl except the maternal uncle of Abu al-Tahir ibn Sarh: Wathimah ibn Musa ibn Rabiah."
"1922","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Abu Humaydah al-Zaini, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Bishr ibn Bakr; Abu al-Tahir was alone in narrating it."
"1923","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Qudamah, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Amr ibn Aws, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rakahs, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two before Asr, and two before Fajr. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qudamah except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ubayd Allah ibn al-Munkadir was alone in narrating it."
"1924","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Nubayt, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon upon a red camel. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Nubayt except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"1925","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, what do you say about me? He said: And what could I say about you? He said: I work with the pen. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The master of the pen will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in a chest of fire locked upon him with locks of fire; if he used it in obedience to Allah and seeking His pleasure, the chest will be opened for him, and if he used it in disobedience to Allah, the chest will plunge with him seventy autumns, even the shaper of the pen and the attacher of the inkwell. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ismail ibn Ayyash; Abu Yusuf was alone in narrating it."
"1926","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Abd Allah ibn Kab al-Himyari, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does the fasting person kiss? So he said to him: Ask this one, meaning Umm Salamah; so she informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does that. So he said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven your past and future sins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I am the most God-fearing of you toward Allah and the most knowledgeable of you of His limits. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his mother Umm Salamah, except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Harith was alone in narrating it."
"1927","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami narrated to him, that he heard his father Hamzah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the hump of every camel is a devil, so when you ride them, glorify Allah, and do not fall short of your need. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Hamzah except Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi."
"1928","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd al-Salam al-Sadafi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sinan ibn Sad, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Islam began strange, and it will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Ibn Wahb."
"1929","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhayl ibn Malik narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out preparing an army, and he looked at al-Abbas and said: This is al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn al-Musayyib except Abu Suhayl ibn Malik."
"1930","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Mulayl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Umayyah, that Habib ibn Maslamah came to Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah during the first fitnah while he was upon a horse, so he stepped back from the saddle for him, and said to him: Ride, but he refused to ride. So Qays said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front. So Habib said: I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, but I fear for you. This hadith is not narrated from Habib ibn Maslamah except with this chain; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1931","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Razin al-Ghafiqi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the one who deliberately passes in front of a man while he is praying will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he were a dry tree. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1932","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Qays, from his father, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people during the Farewell Hajj, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, take your rites, for I do not know, perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this year of mine. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Dawud ibn Qays, nor from Dawud except his son Sulayman, nor from Sulayman except Ibn Abi Fudayk; al-Munkadiri was alone in narrating it."
"1933","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Harami ibn Umarah and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi."
"1934","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl ibn Khalid al-Rabai narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Mishrah ibn Haan, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed those who come to women in their anuses. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Lahiah except Ibn Wahb; Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl was alone in narrating it."
"1935","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I am amazed at a people who sought this knowledge until, when they attained some of it, they became guardians for the sons of kings."
"1936","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever remains silent is saved."
"1937","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Waqqasi, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to be safe, let him adhere to silence. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in narrating it."
"1938","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Sahl, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever teaches his son the Quran by looking, Allah forgives him his past and future sins; and whoever teaches it to him outwardly, Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon, and it will be said to his son: Recite; so every time he recites a verse, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, raises the father a degree by it, until he reaches the end of what he has of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Umar ibn Sahl; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in narrating it."
"1939","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub al-Huraqi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Shaban is halfway, then break fast. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except his son al-Munkadir; his son Abd Allah was alone in narrating it."
"1940","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, that Abd Allah ibn Abbas informed him that he used to teach Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and he mentioned the long hadith of al-Saqifah, and mentioned therein: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not praise me excessively as the Christians excessively praised Isa, for I am only the servant of Allah and His Messenger, so say: The servant of Allah and His Messenger. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned with him. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except Khalid ibn Nizar."
"1941","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Abi Najiyah al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Yaqub ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abbas, when he prayed over funerals as imam, would say takbir, then recite the Mother of the Quran, then send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then say takbir, then depart. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yaqub ibn Zayd, nor from Yaqub except Muhammad ibn Jafar; Ziyad ibn Yunus was alone in narrating it."
"1942","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim ibn Mathrud al-Ghafiqi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Abu al-Munayb, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to pray in trousers with nothing else on him. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; Ibn Wahb was alone in narrating it."
"1943","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, he said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik in his tent during the caliphate of Abd al-Malik, and I said to him: I hope that Allah only kept you back to be a witness against this ummah. He said: So I bear witness that they have entered evening and morning contradicting those before them, because they pray, and in the prayer there is delay. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar except Al-Nadr ibn Muhammad."
"1944","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi informed me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. Then he fell silent, so they said: In what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He employs him in righteous work before he dies. None narrated it from Usamah except Ibn Wahb."
"1945","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, from Bukayr, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every good deed the son of Adam does is multiplied ten times, up to seven hundredfold, except fasting; it is Mine, and I reward for it. None narrated it from Bukayr except Amr."
"1946","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Humran informed me, from Kharijah ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to me: Shall I not teach you a word the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me? I said: Yes, O uncle. He said: When the Messenger of Allah stayed as my guest, he said: Shall I not teach you a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: Say often: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Kharijah ibn Abd Allah except Yunus ibn Humran; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in narrating it."
"1947","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, in marfu form, he said: Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim; so whoever can pray witr with five, let him pray witr; whoever cannot pray witr with five, let him pray witr with three; whoever cannot with three, let him pray witr with one; and whoever cannot pray witr with one, let him gesture with a gesture. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Abu Muawiyah."
"1948","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad, from al-Hasan, from Abu Dharr, that he met Umar ibn al-Khattab, took his hand and squeezed it, and Umar was a strong man, so he said: Release my hand, O lock of fitnah. So Umar said: And what is the lock of fitnah? He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was sitting with people gathered around him, so I sat at the end of them; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fitnah will befall you as long as this one is among you. No one narrated this hadith from Al-Sari ibn Yahya except Abu Muawiyah."
"1949","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: If you had seen us with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you would have thought our scent was the scent of sheep; our clothing was only wool, and our food was the two black ones: water and dates. Abu Salamah is Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah. None narrated this hadith except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"1950","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn al-Qaqa, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: O people, I forbid you from al-zur; and he came with a black rag, cast it before them, and said: It is this, which a woman puts on her head. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn al-Qaqa except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"1951","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Al-Mualla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, supports this religion with peoples who have no share in it. No one narrated this hadith from Al-Mualla ibn Ziyad except Hammad ibn Zayd; Hudbah was alone in narrating it."
"1952","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: Indeed al-umra is permissible."
"1953","And from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not mix raisins with dates, nor unripe dates with dates, meaning nabidh. None narrated these two hadiths from Malik ibn Dinar except Bistam ibn Muslim; Abu Dawud was alone in narrating them."
"1954","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi and Abu Sawrah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves his brother of a distress among the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress among the distresses of the Hereafter; and Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sawrah except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1955","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Munim ibn Nuaym al-Riyahi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan and from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal: When you call the adhan, proceed slowly in your adhan, and when you call the iqamah, hasten; and place between your adhan and your iqamah the measure of time in which the eater finishes his food, the drinker his drink, and the one who enters to relieve himself; and do not stand until you see me."
"1956","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Aidh al-Tai, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: The people of apostasy from Asad and Ghatafan came to Abu Bakr after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), asking him for a truce. So he said: On condition that we strip you of weapons and horses, and you be left following the tails of cattle, until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, shows the caliph of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the believers a view by which they excuse you; and you testify that our slain are in Paradise and your slain are in Hell, and you pay blood money for our slain, and we do not pay blood money for your slain. So Umar said: O caliph of the Messenger of Allah, the statement is as you said, except that our slain were killed in the path of Allah and there is no blood money for them. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Aidh except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"1957","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Dawud Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, he said: A woman of the women of Al-Husayn ibn Ali prepared food on some of his land, so he tasted it, then the food was lifted; then a freed slave of his came, so he called for the food, and he said: O Abu Abd Allah, I do not want it. He said: Why? He said: We ate just now with Ubayd Allah ibn al-Abbas. So Al-Husayn said: Indeed his father was the chief of Quraysh; indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, feed food. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Amr ibn Thabit; Abu Attab was alone in narrating it."
"1958","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Ziyad, the freed slave of Uthman ibn Affan, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant will never believe until he believes in qadar, its good and its evil, and knows that what befell him was never going to miss him, and what missed him was never going to befall him. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Ziyad except Abd Allah ibn Jafar."
"1959","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Ghudani narrated to us, he said: Al-Mualla ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted nabidh of the jar after having forbidden it."
"1960","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna, the brother of Abu Musa, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Shaqiq ibn Abd Allah ibn Umayr al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, that he came with a water-skin from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had washed his face, rinsed in it, spat into the water, washed his hands and forearms, then filled the water-skin, and said: Do not come to any water but that you pour the water-skin over what remains in it; then when you reach your land, sprinkle that spot with it and take it as a mosque. He said: So they took it as such. Amr said: And I prayed in it. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Umayr al-Sadusi except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna was alone in narrating it."
"1961","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah, from Anas, he said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab died and they wanted to bring him out at night, Ibn Umar said: If you delayed him until morning, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It rises with the two horns of Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Sayyar except Hushaym."
"1962","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Salim, he said: I heard Amir al-Shabi saying: I heard Abu Juhayfah... Shall I inform you of the best of the ummah after its Prophet? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: Abu Bakr. Then he said: O Abu Juhayfah, shall I inform you of the best of the ummah after Abu Bakr? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: O Abu Juhayfah, shall I inform you of the best of it after Umar? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: Another man; he did not name him. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Salim except Hushaym; Al-Hasan ibn Ali was alone in narrating it."
"1963","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Rashid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Salim informed me, he said: Alqamah ibn Wail narrated to me, from his father Wail ibn Hujr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man who had killed a person was brought to him, so he handed the killer to the guardian of the slain to kill him; when he went off with him with a leather strap around his neck, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: The killer and the killed are in the Fire. So a man went and mentioned to him what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, so he released him; I saw him when he released him going off dragging his leather strap. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Salim except Hushaym."
"1964","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir al-Dubai narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mikhwal ibn Rashid, from Abu Jafar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Said ibn Amir."
"1965","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umayr al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: ... from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up one night, raised his head to the sky, and began turning his gaze saying: Glory be to Allah, what trials have been sent down tonight, and what treasuries have been opened? Wake the mistresses of the chambers, for many a clothed one in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said and Amr ibn Dinar except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"1966","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umayr al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fortify your wealth with zakah, treat your sick with charity, and prepare supplication for calamity. No one narrated this hadith from Al-Hakam except Musa ibn Umayr."
"1967","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave after it was buried. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, except Hammad ibn Waqid."
"1968","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn al-Mundhir al-Muzani, from Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Nothing breaks the prayer except hadath; and I do not shy away from telling you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not shy away from: Hadath is to pass wind or to break wind loudly. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn ibn al-Mundhir except Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah."
"1969","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakhai narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Ali adjured the people: Who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Do you not know that I am closer to the believers than their own selves? They said: Yes. He said: So whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. So twelve men stood and testified to that. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Sharik and Abu Awanah."
"1970","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a man who buys a sacrificial animal or a camel for sacrifice then sells it and buys a fatter one, and he mentioned a concession. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Sharik."
"1971","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Jabalah ibn Harithah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you go to your bed, recite: Say, O disbelievers, to its end, for it is a declaration of innocence from shirk."
"1972","And from Jabalah ibn Harithah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go on a raid, he would give his weapon to Ali or Usamah. None narrated these two hadiths from Abu Ishaq except Sharik and al-Amash."
"1973","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hurayth, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would warm himself with her after ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Hurayth."
"1974","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad ibn Abd Allah, from Ali: And warn your nearest kindred. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered thirty men over a cup of milk, though most of them would eat a young camel; so they ate until they were full and drank until they were quenched. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Sharik and Abu Awanah."
"1975","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carrying Al-Hasan ibn Ali upon his shoulder, saying: O Allah, indeed I love Hasan, so love him. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Sharik."
"1976","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, in marfu form, he said: He said on the day of Awtas: A pregnant woman is not to be approached until she delivers her pregnancy, nor a non-pregnant one until she menstruates one menstruation. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Wahb except Sharik."
"1977","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah: Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar. He said: A river in Paradise, hollow, in it vessels of gold and silver, which none knows but Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Sharik."
"1978","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the bright-faced and bright-limbed on the Day of Resurrection from the traces of ablution, so whoever among you can extend his brightness, let him do so. No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except Layth; Al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad was alone in narrating it."
"1979","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated to us, he said: My father mentioned, from Anas ibn Malik, I only know it in marfu form, he said: The son of Adam has never met anything since Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, created him harder upon him than death. Then he said: Indeed death is easier than what comes after it; and they will meet such terror of that Day severely until sweat bridles them, until if ships were sailed in it they would sail. None narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz except his son Sukayn."
"1980","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, that a man came to Ibn Masud and said: I read al-Mufassal in one rakah. So Abd Allah said: Rather rapid recitation like the rapid recitation of poetry, or like the scattering of inferior dates; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not do as you did; he used to read al-Nazair: Al-Rahman and Al-Najm in one rakah, with twenty surahs of al-Mufassal, upon the arrangement of Abd Allah, the last of them When the sun is folded up and Al-Dukhan. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zuhayr."
"1981","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Musab ibn Sad, from Sad, if Allah wills, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Aishah excels over women as tharid excels over other foods. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zuhayr."
"1982","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Salim and Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Shabi, that Ali flogged Shurahah on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and said: I flogged her by the Book of Allah, and stoned her by the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Salim except Hushaym."
"1983","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, and Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay across in front of him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Dawud al-Attar; Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad was alone in narrating it."
"1984","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Al-Shabi narrated to us, from Alqamah, that Abd Allah ibn Masud used to stand every Thursday evening, and I never heard him on any evening of them saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, except once; then I looked at him leaning upon a staff, and I looked at the staff shaking."
"1985","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Al-Shabi narrated to me, from Qarazah ibn Kab al-Ansari, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab accompanied us on foot when we set out to Kufah, leading a donkey or she-ass; so we said: O Commander of the Believers, we adjure you to ride, but he refused, until we traveled three or four miles; then some of us said to others: You have burdened the Commander of the Believers; so we dismounted, and one of them said: Why do you think I accompanied you to this place? They said: You intended thereby our honor and preserving the Ansar. He said: Indeed that is so, and besides that, what is it? I said: We do not know. So he said: You will come to a people who will hunger after your narrations, so narrate little from the Messenger of Allah, and I am your partner in that. None narrated these two hadiths from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"1986","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Durust narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about stray camels. So he said: Leave it; it has its shoes and its water-skin; it eats from trees and drinks from water until its owner takes it. So he was asked about stray sheep. So he said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about guarded mountain produce? He said: Its fine and the like of it with it, and floggings as deterrence; then if the resting enclosure shelters it, then whatever reaches the price of a shield, therein is cutting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about hanging fruit? He said: Its fine and the like of it with it, and floggings as deterrence; then when the threshing floor shelters it, then whatever reaches the price of a shield, therein is cutting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a found item that is found? So he said: Whatever is in an inhabited village or a frequented road, announce it for a year; then if you find its owner, otherwise enjoy it. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about buried treasure? He said: In buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Ata except Muhammad ibn Thabit and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali."
"1987","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, so they met the enemy and continued killing until they reached the children; when the detachment returned, that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Did I not forbid you? They said: They are only the children of the polytheists. So he said: Are not your best ones the children of the polytheists? Then he ordered a caller to call: Indeed every newborn is born upon the fitrah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad except Hammad ibn Zayd; Ibn Hisab was alone in narrating it."
"1988","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim Abu Muawiyah al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: How many gods do you worship today? He said: Seven, six on earth and one in heaven. He said: Which of them do you count for your hope and your fear? He said: The one in heaven. So he said: O Husayn, if you become Muslim I will teach you two words that will benefit you. He said: When Husayn became Muslim, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the two words you promised me. He said: So he said: O Allah, inspire me with my right guidance, and protect me from the evil of my soul. No one narrated this hadith from Shabib ibn Shaybah except Abu Muawiyah."
"1989","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Jubayr or Ibn Kathir, Abu al-Rabi doubted, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of a third, for that harms the believer, and Allah, the Exalted, hates harming the believer. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Ibn al-Mubarak was alone in narrating it."
"1990","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs al-Abdi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hand of the Most Merciful is above the head of the muezzin, and he is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, wherever it reaches. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umar ibn Hafs."
"1991","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Al-Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Exalted, wrote a book two thousand years before creating the heavens and the earth, and sent down from it two verses with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah; they are not recited in a house for three nights and then a devil approaches it. This hadith is not narrated from al-Numan except with this chain; Hammad ibn Salamah was alone in narrating it."
"1992","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Qazaah, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I pray upon my riding animal wherever it turns with me? He said: Yes. I said: Is it from the sunnah? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Wuhayb."
"1993","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Sahuli garments, in which there was neither shirt nor turban. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Abi Amr except Al-Darawardi."
"1994","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, the freed slave of Banu Makhzum, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in When the heaven splits asunder and in Read in the name of your Lord. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from al-Araj, except Yazid ibn Abi Habib."
"1995","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Qari, that Ali used to say: I spent a night at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I would hear him, when he finished his prayer and took his bed, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from You; O Allah, I cannot praise You though I strive, but You are as You praised Yourself. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Qari except Yazid ibn Khusayfah; Ismail ibn Jafar was alone in narrating it."
"1996","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying three things about Banu Tamim which I will never cease to love them for: Charity camels of Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: These are the camels of my people, making them his people; and upon Aishah was a vow to free from the offspring of Ismail, so captives from Khawlan came forward, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free from them, for they are from the offspring of Ismail; and they are the severest of people against the Dajjal, meaning Banu Tamim. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Maslamah ibn Alqamah."
"1997","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man walks to a man and kills him, the killed is in Paradise and the killer in Hell. No one narrated this hadith from Raqabah except Awanah."
"1998","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought a battle and did not finish until evening kept him from prayer past the time the Messenger of Allah used to observe; when he finished with them, he looked, and the Asr prayer had entered evening; so he prayed, and when he finished his prayer, he supplicated against his enemy, saying: O Allah, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire."
"1999","And from Ibn Abbas, he said: When: When the help of Allah and the victory comes, the surah, was revealed, the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was announced to him when it was sent down; so he engaged in the most strenuous striving in the matter of the Hereafter; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereafter: The help of Allah has come, and the victory has come, and the people of Yemen have come. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, and what are the people of Yemen? He said: A people whose hearts are tender, whose hearts are soft; faith is Yemeni and understanding is Yemeni."
"2000","And from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his raids, and a man asked him: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the distracted? So he was silent toward him and did not answer him a word; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his raid and prevailed over them, there was a boy who had fallen from his elevated seat, searching in the earth; so a caller called: Where is the questioner? The man came forward until he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing children, then said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"2001","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Juwbari narrated to us, he said: Al-Fadl ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servants stand for reckoning, a people will come with their swords placed upon their necks, dripping blood, and crowd at the gate of Paradise. It will be said: Who are these? It will be said: The martyrs; they were alive, provided for. Then a caller will call: Let whoever has his reward upon Allah stand and enter Paradise. Then he will call a second time: Let whoever has his reward upon Allah stand and enter Paradise. He said: And who is he whose reward is upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic? He said: Those who pardon people. Then he will call a third time: Let whoever has his reward upon Allah stand and enter Paradise. So so many thousands will stand and enter it without reckoning. We do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah except with this chain, and none narrated it except Yahya ibn Khalaf."
"2002","Ahmad ibn Dukayn al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Rabai informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things I will never abandon: He enjoined upon me witr before sleep, enjoined upon me ghusl every Friday, and enjoined upon me fasting three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Rabai except Humayd al-Kindi."
"2003","Ahmad ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when the Master of the Trumpet has taken the trumpet in his mouth and bent his forehead, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what should we say? He said: Say: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and none narrated it from Sufyan except Rawh ibn Ubadah and Zuhayr ibn Abbad."
"2004","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Maymun al-Marai narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan ibn Qudamah, he said: My father Safwan emigrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Madinah, and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended his hand to him and wiped over it; so Safwan said to him: I love you, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: A man is with whom he loves. This hadith is not narrated from Safwan except with this chain; Musa ibn Maymun was alone in narrating it, from his father."
"2005","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Maymun ibn Musa al-Marai narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me; Allah has made a way for them: The virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and exile; and the previously married with the previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Musa except his son Musa ibn Maymun and Yazid ibn Harun."
"2006","Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My uncle Al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: Jafar ibn Abi Talib came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the land of Abyssinia, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed between his eyes and said: I do not know whether I am happier by the arrival of Jafar or by the conquest of Khaybar. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Makhlad; Al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik was alone in narrating it."
"2007","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghiyath al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sadi al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qasri al-Muallim narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya Ayyub ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, none of us would bend his back until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, then we would prostrate after him. This hadith is not narrated from Ibrahim al-Saigh except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sadi was alone in narrating it."
"2008","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghafrah al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Aishah bint Arar, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the talbiyah: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; indeed praise, blessing, and dominion are Yours; no partner have You. None narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd except Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghafrah and Ali ibn al-Madini."
"2009","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili Abu Yala narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed a righteous trait may be in a man, so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, rectifies all his deeds by it; and a man's purification for his prayer expiates his sins through it, while his prayer remains as supererogatory for him. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah except with this chain, and none narrated it from Thabit except Bashshar ibn al-Hakam."
"2010","Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ziyad al-Jabali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Wahb Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayd al-Kalai narrated to us, from Makhul, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: He transmitted a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you comes to Friday, let him bathe. It is not narrated from the hadith of Makhul except from al-Hawti."
"2011","Ahmad ibn Bishr ibn Habib al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: Al-Abbas ibn Ismail al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim. None narrated it except Muhammad ibn Musaffa."
"2012","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn al-Walid ibn Abd Allah ibn Jumay al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Said ibn Zayd, and he was a Badri, that he was sitting with al-Mughirah ibn Shubah when a man came and spoke ill of Ali; so Said became angry and said: Are the companions of the Messenger of Allah spoken ill of in your presence? So I bear witness that Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Sad is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise; and if I wished to name the ninth I would name him. So the people said to him and pressed him: Inform us. So he said: And I am in Paradise; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was upon Hira and it shook, strike it with his foot, then say: Be still, O Hira, for there is none upon you but a Prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr; and these people were with him. None narrated it except Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami."
"2013","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn Abu Jafar al-Ansari al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ghalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Ghalib al-Sadi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, a man of the Ansar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Abu Bakr. None narrated it from Sufyan except this shaykh Ghalib; and he contradicted Shubah, for Shubah narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Ali."
"2014","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that some people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We go far from water for three months and five, and find no water, and among us are the menstruating, the junub, and the postpartum? He said: Upon you is the earth. We do not know of Sulayman al-Ahwal from Said ibn al-Musayyib other than this, and none narrated it except Waki, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid. And it was narrated from Said ibn al-Musayyib by another route, and al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated it from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Said."
"2015","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Madini al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a stone that used to greet me before I was sent; indeed I know it now. No one narrated it from Shubah except Yahya ibn Said, and none narrated it from Yahya except Zayd ibn al-Harish."
"2016","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Salih narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came with dinars and cast them into the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so the Messenger of Allah began turning them over, saying: Nothing Uthman does after this day will harm him. None narrated it except Zayd ibn al-Harish, from Amr ibn Salih, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"2017","Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month until you see the crescent, or complete the number before it. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam."
"2018","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri, Hammad ibn Salamah, and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man swears and says: If Allah wills, he has made an exception. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Al-Husayn ibn al-Walid."
"2019","Ahmad ibn Said ibn Urwah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhayl ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever peeks into the house of a people without their permission, it becomes lawful for them to put out his eye. None narrated it from Abu Suhayl except Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai. And it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah by other routes: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated it from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated it from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"2020","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isam ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; rather let him be resolute in asking, for none compels Him. No one narrated it from al-Amash except Sufyan, and none narrated it from Sufyan except Muhammad."
"2021","Ahmad ibn Jafar Abu Hamid al-Mulhami al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Natifi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Say, I do not ask you for any reward except that you guard me regarding kinship, that you not belie me nor harm me. None narrated it from Abu Sad al-Baqqal except Abu Zuhayr."
"2022","Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Ayyub al-Madini al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabiah, he said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) face the Stone and kiss it, then say: By Allah, I know you are a stone that owns neither harm nor benefit for me; and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not have kissed you. None narrated it from Mansur except Abu Hamzah."
"2023","Ahmad ibn Rustah ibn Umar al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hanifah, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, that a man of the Ansar passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was grieving, and the man had food to which people gathered, and he entered his mosque praying; while thus, he dozed, and one came to him in sleep and said: I know what grieved you; then he mentioned the story of the adhan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr has informed us of the like of that, so command Bilal to call the adhan with that. None narrated it from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Abu Hanifah."
"2024","Ahmad ibn Surayj al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah al-Shairi narrated to us, he said: Al-Salt ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Shimr, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn in your prayers, for there is no prayer for one who turns. None narrated it from Al-Salt ibn Thabit except Abu Qutaybah, and it is not narrated from the Prophet except with this chain."
"2025","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Malik al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed these dinars and dirhams destroyed those before you, and I see them only destroying you."
"2026","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Jurashi, narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Day when some of the signs of your Lord come. He said: The rising of the sun from its west. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman except Abu Uways; Al-Nadr ibn Muhammad was alone in narrating it."
"2027","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Humran ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu al-Muhazzam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah, and a legion of locusts met us, so we struck at them with our whips and sticks; then we were perplexed about that, so we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: There is no harm in sea game. Abu Salamah is Hammad ibn Salamah, and none narrated it except Ali ibn Bahr, from this shaykh of his."
"2028","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi and Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in prayer for the tashahhud, he placed his hands upon his knees, then raised his index finger next to the thumb, with the rest of the fingers of his right hand clenched as they were. None narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, except Hisham ibn Yusuf, from Mamar."
"2029","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The briber and the bribed are in the Fire. None narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj except Ali ibn Bahr, from Hisham."
"2030","Ahmad ibn Musa al-Shami al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Mihran al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah said: What do you call those who enter among you from the people of the villages, having among you neither lineage nor kinship? I said: We call them al-uluj and al-siqat. So Aishah said: We used to call them al-muhajirun in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Humayd ibn Mihran."
"2031","Ahmad ibn al-Khidr al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abu Muadh al-Nahwi narrated to us, saying: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Salm ibn Bashir, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take the sahur meal, for indeed in sahur there is blessing. No one narrated it from Raqabah except Abu Hamzah."
"2032","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Khuwarazmi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Zuhri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow except in that through which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is obeyed, and there is no oath in anger, and there is no emancipation nor divorce in that which one does not own. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Sulayman; Umar ibn Yunus alone transmitted it."
"2033","Ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Khuwarazmi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ali ibn Husayn ibn Ali, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim. It is not narrated from al-Husayn ibn Ali except through this chain."
"2034","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Ataki narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perfume himself with the best perfume he could find when he entered ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sad except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra."
"2035","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hakam ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Abd al-Hakam ibn Maysarah alone transmitted it."
"2036","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hakam ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, and wipe over his turban, and wipe over his two leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Qays; Abd al-Hakam ibn Maysarah alone transmitted it."
"2037","Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish the prayer, give the zakat, perform hajj and umrah, and be upright, you will be set upright. We did not write it except from this shaykh."
"2038","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Hunai narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Abu al-Zibriqan al-Hilali, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad, it is as if he recited a third of the Quran. This hadith is not narrated from Yazid, from Anas, except with this chain; Zayd ibn Akhzam alone transmitted it."
"2039","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Madari narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells date-palms that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the master, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Amr ibn Asim; Ibn Zayd alone transmitted it, and he is trustworthy."
"2040","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Sakan Abu Khurasan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat from a shoulder, then prayed, and did not perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ammar, nor from Ammar except Abu al-Jawwab; Abu Khurasan al-Baghdadi alone transmitted it, and he was trustworthy."
"2041","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir al-Jufi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I saw Sad ibn Malik pray witr with one rakah, then he said: This is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl except Jabir; Abu Hamzah Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Sukkari alone transmitted it."
"2042","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad Abu al-Rabi al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, saying: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in Iqra bi-smi Rabbik. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except al-Layth ibn Sad; Bishr ibn Umar alone transmitted it."
"2043","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wishes, let him ask much, for he is only asking his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Ubayd Allah ibn Musa."
"2044","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Mihran ibn Abi Umar al-Razi narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The voluntary night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was thirteen rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Mihran."
"2045","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was a girl of six, and I was brought to him when I was a girl of nine, and I stayed with him nine years. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu al-Jawwab."
"2046","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar al-Ayli narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, saying: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, saying: Jabir ibn Yazid al-Jufi narrated to me, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: I found two dinars, so I brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Announce them for a year. So I announced them for a year, then I brought them back to him, and he said: Guard its container, its tie, and its count, and benefit from it, and when its owner comes, return it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"2047","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, that Usamah ibn Zayd, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, did not come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for days, then he came to him, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him, he wept, and he said to him: You were absent from us as long as you were absent, then you came grieving us. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq."
"2048","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It has been reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the children of the polytheists that he said to Aishah: If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to let you hear their crying out in the Fire; and it has been reported from him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done. So the matter returns to his saying (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah knows best what they would have done: whoever Allah's prior knowledge holds that had he grown up he would not have believed, he is the one about whom he said to Aishah: If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah to let you hear their crying out in the Fire; and whoever Allah's prior knowledge holds that had he grown up he would have believed, they are those about whom he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are servants of the people of Paradise. Thus the meanings of the three hadiths are established, and this is the saying of Ahl al-Sunnah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Raja except Abbad ibn Mansur."
"2049","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a donkey on his way to Khaybar, with the qiblah behind him. Abu al-Qasim said: Meaning that he was praying voluntary prayer on the donkey, just as he prays on the riding mount."
"2050","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon his companions while they were conversing and talking, and they said: We were mentioning what we were in during Jahiliyyah, and how Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guided us, and what misguidance we were in. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have done well, and it pleased him; be like this, or: do like this. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Mubarak."
"2051","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: I entered upon Umar and he said: O Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, do you fear that people will abandon Islam and leave it? I said: No, Allah willing; how would they abandon it when among them is the Book of Allah and the sunnahs of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: If anything of that happens, it will surely be the sons of so-and-so."
"2052","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Hatim ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to archery, for it is the best of your play."
"2053","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he bowed place his palms on his knees and spread his fingers. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi."
"2054","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, saying: Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) measured out a handspan for her from her hem. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus and Humayd except Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except Fahd ibn Awf; Ibrahim ibn Rashid alone transmitted it."
"2055","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated to us, saying: Fahd ibn Awf Abu Rabiah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Asim al-Ahwal and Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: I asked Abu Said al-Khudri about vessels? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vessels, except what was tied shut among waterskins."
"2056","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Umayr ibn Abd al-Majid Abu al-Mughirah al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Rafi ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah: a man selling his date-palms for such-and-such wasqs of dates for such-and-such wasqs of fresh dates; if there is excess it belongs to the buyer, and if there is deficiency it is upon the buyer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Aswad ibn al-Ala al-Madani except Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar."
"2057","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Wahb, who said: Khabbab narrated to me, saying: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the heat of the ground, and he did not relieve our complaint, and he said: When the sun passes its zenith, pray zuhr. Abu al-Qasim said: No one among those who narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq said: When the sun passes its zenith, pray zuhr, except Yunus; Abu Bakr al-Hanafi alone transmitted it, and his name is Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid."
"2058","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but the brotherhood of Islam is better."
"2059","And with its chain: from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Close the doors that open into the mosque, except the door of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2060","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, saying: Abu Rabiah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Habib ibn al-Shahid and Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dreams are a part of forty-six parts of prophethood, and the dream of the believer hardly errs at the end of time."
"2061","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in solitude, no rider would ever travel by night, nor would a man sleep alone in a house."
"2062","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abu Hammad al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Hayyaj al-Asadi, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, sent me and said: Do you know for what I am sending you? For that for which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me; he said: Do not leave an image except that you break it, nor a raised grave except that you level it."
"2063","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forbidden through breastfeeding is what is forbidden through lineage."
"2064","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti al-Daqiqi, brother of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man said: Alhamdu lillah kathiran, and the angel deemed it too great to write, and he referred it to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and it was said to him: Write it as My servant said, kathiran."
"2065","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Madhari narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Surayj al-Bazzaz narrated to us, saying: I said to Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn: May I be sacrificed for you, do you see this intercession that the people of Iraq speak of, is it true? He said: Intercession of what? He said: The intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: True, by Allah; by Allah, my uncle Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will intercede for my ummah until my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, calls to me and says: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? And I will say: Yes, I am pleased."
"2066","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil Yahya ibn Habib ibn Abd Allah ibn Habib ibn Thabit narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: al-Fadl ibn Dalham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, and the woman who tattoos and the one for whom it is done. A woman said: Among his family is one who does that. He said: Go and look. So she looked and saw nothing."
"2067","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Ghalib narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to me, saying: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan comes to one of you in prayer and says: You have passed wind, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"2068","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the day of Arafah is expiation for the past year and the coming year."
"2069","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah and al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: I used to comb the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was menstruating."
"2070","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: al-Abbas ibn Yazid al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning sciatica: The fat of the tail of an Arabian ram, neither small nor large, is taken, melted, and drunk for three days on an empty stomach. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn al-Shahid except Abd al-Khaliq."
"2071","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Habhabi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Hamzah ibn Amr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling? He said: Fast if you wish, and break fast if you wish."
"2072","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Bishr ibn Mansur al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no servant who has wealth and does not pay its zakat except that it will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, plates of Hellfire heated upon him, and his side and back branded therewith, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path: either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakat except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as they ever were passing before him, then he will be laid flat on a smooth level plain, then the first of them and the last of them will run over him; whenever the first of them passes, the last returns, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose measure was fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path: either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of livestock who does not pay their zakat except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as numerous as they ever were, and he will be laid flat on a smooth plain, and they will trample him with their hooves and butt him with their horns; among them there is no curly-horned, nor broken-horned, nor hornless one; whenever the last of them passes, the first is returned upon him, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose measure was fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path: either to Paradise or to the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about horses? He said: Good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and horses are for three: for one man a reward, for another a cover, and upon another a burden. As for the one for whom it is a reward: a man who keeps it and prepares it in the path of Allah; whatever is hidden in their bellies is reward for him, and were he to graze them in a meadow, he would have reward in what is hidden in their bellies, and were they to run a hill or two, he would have reward for every step they take, and were a river to come before him and he gives them to drink from it, he would have reward for every drop they hide in their bellies, so much so that it is mentioned even in their dung and urine. And as for that which is a cover for him: a man who takes them for self-sufficiency, dignity, and honor, and does not forget the right of their backs and bellies in hardship and ease. And as for that which is a burden upon him: a man who takes them in arrogance and insolence, or to show off to people, and in pride over them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about donkeys? He said: Nothing was revealed to me concerning them except this comprehensive, singular verse: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it."
"2073","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Makhlad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dye his beard yellow. No one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except Makhlad; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr alone transmitted it."
"2074","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Madhari narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that Abu Thalabah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the delegation of Yemen, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where nothing suits us except drink, and there is a drink made from honey called bit, and a drink from grain called mizr? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forbidden is a small amount of that whose large amount intoxicates. No one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except Hammam."
"2075","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring and the iron ring. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hammam."
"2076","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays Abu Zukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt. No one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except Abu Zukayr."
"2077","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, saying: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who among people has the best voice in reciting the Quran? He said: The one whom, when you hear his recitation, you see that he fears Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated it from Misar except Humayd ibn Hammad; Muhammad ibn Mamar alone transmitted it."
"2078","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a mat. No one narrated it from Hisham except Hammad ibn Masadah. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays."
"2079","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Waki narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyyah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me for household goods worth forty dirhams. No one narrated it from Fudayl except Waki."
"2080","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Abbad narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Maiz, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrating, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Urine is not to be left to soak in a basin in the house, for the angels do not enter a house in which urine is left soaking, and do not urinate in your bathing place. It is not narrated from Ibn Yazid except with this chain; Yahya ibn Abbad alone transmitted it."
"2081","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no man who attends Friday without engaging in idle talk or ignorance, performs ablution well, and attends it with the imam, except that it is expiation between it and the next Friday; nor does he pray an obligatory prayer except that it is expiation between it and the next prayer. No one narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah except Dawud ibn Abd al-Hamid; Ishaq al-Baghawi alone transmitted it."
"2082","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Abu Abbad Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the place of the lower garment? He took hold of the muscle of my leg and said: Up to here; if you refuse, then the lower garment has no right below that. No one narrated it from Malik ibn Mighwal except Yahya ibn Abbad."
"2083","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that he said on the day of Ashura: We used to fast it, then it was left. No one narrated it from Sufyan except al-Ashjai. And the explanation of the saying of Ibn Masud, we used to fast it, then it was left, is: we used to fast it as obligatory, then it became voluntary."
"2084","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sasah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not pass on the night I was taken up on a company of angels except that they commanded me with cupping. No one narrated it from Qatadah except Hammam, nor from Hammam except Amr ibn Asim; Abd al-Quddus alone transmitted it."
"2085","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Sufyan al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Jahm al-Razi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a company of Ansar shooting at a pigeon, and said: Do not take a living soul as a target. No one narrated it from Mansur except Amr ibn Abi Qays; Abd Allah ibn al-Jahm alone transmitted it."
"2086","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, saying: al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from al-Qartha, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these four rakahs you pray at midday? He said: This is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and they are not closed until zuhr is prayed, so I love to send forth good. No one narrated it from Said ibn Masruq except al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah; Ali ibn Thabit alone transmitted it."
"2087","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Friday was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Jibril came with something in his palm like a white mirror, in whose middle was like a black dot, and he said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Friday; your Lord presents it to you so that it be a festival for you and for your people after you, and for you therein is good: you are first, and the Jews and Christians are after you, and therein is an hour in which no one supplicates his Lord for good allotted to him except that He gives him, or seeks refuge from evil except that He averts from him what is greater than it; and we call it in the Hereafter the Day of Increase, and that is because your Lord has taken in Paradise a wide valley of white musk, and when it is Friday He descends from Illiyyin, sits upon His Kursi, and the Kursi is surrounded by pulpits of gold crowned with jewels, and the truthful and the martyrs come and sit upon them, and the people of the chambers come from their chambers until they sit upon the hill, which is a white hill of the most fragrant musk, then He manifests Himself to them and says: I am the One who fulfilled My promise to you, completed My blessing upon you, and this is the place of My honor, so ask Me. So they ask Him for good pleasure, and He says: My good pleasure has settled you in My abode and granted you My honor, so ask Me. So they ask Him for good pleasure, and He bears witness to them of good pleasure, then He opens for them what no eye has seen, and what has not occurred to a human heart, until the time of their dispersal from Friday; and it is a green peridot or a red ruby, with its rivers flowing, its fruits hanging, wherein are their spouses and servants; and they are not in Paradise more eager for anything than for Friday, to increase in looking at their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and His honor, and for that it is called the Day of Increase. No one narrated it from Abu Imran except Abd al-Salam; Khalid alone transmitted it."
"2088","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Hawshab ibn Aqil, that a man narrated a hadith in the presence of al-Hasan, and al-Hasan said: Who narrated this to you? He said: The jurists. He said: Have you ever seen a jurist with your eyes? Then he said: Do you know who the jurist is? The jurist is the one ascetic in this world, desirous of the Hereafter, insightful in this religion, holding fast to knowledge."
"2089","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abd Allah ibn Amr, how will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they differ and become like this, and he interlaced his fingers? He said: What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Adhere to what you know, leave what you disapprove, adhere to your own self, and beware of their common folk."
"2090","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Qaysi narrated to us, saying: I heard a shaykh from Ghifar, kunya Abu Abd Allah, narrating from Sahl ibn Sad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril, peace be upon him, commanded me with the siwak until I thought I would lose my teeth. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl except with this chain; Ubayd ibn Waqid alone transmitted it."
"2091","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, saying: al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: An imam kunya Abu Rimthah led us in Asr in our prayer place, and with us was a man who had witnessed the first takbirah; when Abu Rimthah finished, the man stood to add an extra rakah, so Abu Rimthah looked at him and said: I prayed this prayer, or one like this prayer, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar used to be put forward in prayer; and there was a man who had witnessed the first takbirah of the prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then gave salam to right and left, until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks, then he turned as Abu Rimthah turned, meaning himself, faced the people, and the man who had caught the first takbirah with him stood to add; Umar stood to him, took him by the shoulder, pushed him, then said: Sit, for nothing destroyed the People of the Book except that their prayers had no separation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze to him and said: Allah has guided you right, O son of al-Khattab. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rimthah except with this chain; al-Minhal alone transmitted it."
"2092","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, who said: Jami ibn Abi Rashid narrated to me, his tears flowing, from Umm Mubashshir, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When evil appears in the land, Allah sends His punishment upon the people of the land. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if among them are righteous? He said: Yes, even if among them are righteous; what befalls people befalls them, then they return to the mercy of Allah. No one narrated it from Jami except Zubayd, nor from Zubayd except Muhammad ibn Talhah; Hashim ibn al-Qasim alone transmitted it."
"2093","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, saying: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn Urwah, both from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: Barirah was under a slave; she was freed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put her affair in her hand. No one narrated it from Hisham except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"2094","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu Talhah Musa ibn Abd Allah al-Khuzai narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man wore a suit like the suit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then came to a household of Madinah and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me that whichever household I wish, I inspect. They said: Our covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that he does not command indecencies. He said: So they prepared a house for him, and sent a messenger to the Messenger of Allah, who informed him; he said to Abu Bakr and Umar: Go to him; if you find him alive, kill him, then burn him with fire, and if you find that you have been spared him, burn him; I do not see but that you have been spared him. So they came to him and found him gone out in the night to urinate; a viper snake bit him and he died, so they burned him with fire, then returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated it from Ata except Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except Ahmad ibn Ishaq; Abu Talhah alone transmitted it."
"2095","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Ghifari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken up to heaven, I did not pass a heaven except that I found therein my name: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq behind me."
"2096","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Rabi Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is not made impure by anything. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miqdam except Sharik."
"2097","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Kurdi al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam from prayer, he said: O Allah, You are al-Salam, and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh except Qays; Yahya ibn Ishaq alone transmitted it."
"2098","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded himself in a garden, and a man of faint voice came and gave salam, and he said: Give him permission, and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I opened, and there was Abu Bakr, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he praised Allah and sat. Then another came and gave salam, and he said: Give him permission, and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I opened, and there was Umar, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another came and gave salam, and he said: Give him permission, and give him glad tidings of Paradise after a trial that will befall him. So I opened the door, and there was Uthman, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he praised Allah, then sat. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Imran except Said ibn Abi Arubah."
"2099","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who said: Quraysh gathered in Dar al-Nadwah and mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); some said: A sorcerer. They said: He is not a sorcerer. Some said: A soothsayer. They said: He is not a soothsayer. Some said: Mad. They said: He is not mad. They said: He separates between a loved one and his loved one. The polytheists concluded upon that. It reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he was wrapped in his clothes and covered, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: O you enwrapped, O you covered. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Aqil except Sharik; Mualla alone transmitted it."
"2100","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Yaqub ibn Ishaq Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, saying: Khabbab, freedman of Banu Layth, narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, I have a right upon you, and the imams of Quraysh have a right upon you, so long as they uphold three: when mercy is sought from them, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they covenant, they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Khabbab; Bakr ibn al-Aswad alone transmitted it."
"2101","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Harb al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdhah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from his father Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of every month, and sometimes he delayed that until the fast of the year gathered upon him, and sometimes he delayed it until he fasted Shaban. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla except with this chain; Amr alone transmitted it."
"2102","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Hubaysh ibn al-Ward narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Yunus ibn Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"2103","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani al-Kufi narrated to me, that al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to him, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Ukaym al-Juhani narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to them in the land of Juhaynah: Do not benefit from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"2104","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, that Qusaym, freedman of Umarah ibn Utbah, narrated to him, that Qazaah narrated to him, that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and no fasting on the day of the two Eids, and no woman travels more than three nights except with a mahram over her, and saddles are not tied except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, this mosque of mine, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa. No one narrated this hadith from Qusaym, freedman of Umarah, except Aban ibn Salih, nor from Aban except Ibn Ishaq."
"2105","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Be moderate in your prostrations, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads in prostration; by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow and prostrate. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Yaqub ibn Ibrahim."
"2106","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Bishr, maternal brother of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hudayr, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, who said: In Barirah there were four sunnahs: her husband divorced her, and he was a slave, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her choice, and commanded her to observe the waiting period of a free woman; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: Do you have anything to feed us? They said: No, except some meat given in charity to Barirah, which she gifted to us. He said: It is charity upon her, and a gift for us. So he ate from it. And her masters stipulated that they would not sell her except that wala be theirs, so he said: Buy her and free her, for wala belongs to the one who paid the price. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Hudayr except Hammad ibn Masadah."
"2107","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Awf, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Attend to the Quran, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, it is more fleeting from the chests of men than hobbled camels to their resting places. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Hushaym; Ishaq ibn Shahin alone transmitted it."
"2108","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad Abu al-Rabi al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad equals a third of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Imran al-Qasir except Hammad ibn Masadah."
"2109","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Khallad ibn Yazid al-Bahili narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: Which Islam is best? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe. It was said: And which jihad is best? He said: The one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. It was said: Then which prayer is best? He said: Length of standing. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah."
"2110","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Hisham ibn al-Fadl ibn Dalham al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, who said: Ibn Masud was asked, and it was said to him: A man married his wife, did not assign her dowry, and died before consummating with her? He said: I have heard nothing about it; return to me and I will consider it. So they returned, then came to him, and he said: I will say in it with praiseworthy opinion; if I am right, Allah has guided me, and if I err, the error is from me: I see for her the like of the dowry of her womenfolk, neither diminished nor excessive; she has inheritance, and upon her is waiting period. Maqil ibn Sinan al-Ashjai said: He bears witness upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he heard him judge with what you judged in a woman among them called Barwa bint Washiq. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"2111","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Juhani narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that a woman used to come to Ibn Masud for a month, each time he turned her away; her husband had died without assigning her dowry. Abd Allah said: I say in it by opinion; if it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is wrong, it is from Ibn Umm Abd: she has the dowry of one of her womenfolk, and she has inheritance, a fourth and an eighth. And with him was a man from Ashja among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I call Allah to witness, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with it in a woman among us called Barwa bint Washiq. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Wuhayb; Ahmad ibn Ishaq alone transmitted it."
"2112","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr Dhu Murr, who said: I heard Ali adjuring the people: Whoever heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla, let him stand. So twelve stood and bore witness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except his son Abd Allah."
"2113","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from his father, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Umayrah ibn Sad, who said: I heard Ali adjuring the people: Who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla? So thirteen stood and bore witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except his son Abd Allah."
"2114","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yazdad Abu al-Saqr narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Jabir, that a man from the Ansar, kunya Abu Madhkur, freed a slave of his after his death; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him and sold him. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Ibn Abi Najih; Jarir ibn Hazim alone transmitted it."
"2115","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three days, except over a husband. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal alone transmitted it."
"2116","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Bashmin, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves snakes fearing retaliation is not from us. No one narrated this hadith from Bashmin, grandfather of Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani, except Ammar; Abu al-Jawwab alone transmitted it."
"2117","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uthmani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad al-Muadhdhin narrated to us, saying: Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the mirror of the believer. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abd Allah except Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad; Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman alone transmitted it."
"2118","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant benefits after Islam better for him than a believing wife: when he looks at her she pleases him, and when he is absent from her she guards him in herself and his wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Sharik; Yazid alone transmitted it."
"2119","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The wedding feast on the first day is a right, the second is kindness, and the third is showing off and seeking repute. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn."
"2120","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Susi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Qarazah ibn Kab, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, escorted us and said: Reduce narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I am your partner. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata."
"2121","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments, one of them a shirt. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad, nor from Hammad except Muslim; Ibn Aqil alone transmitted it."
"2122","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, saying: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to allegiance on the day of Hudaybiyah; Abu Sinan ibn Mihsan came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I pledge to you upon what is in your soul. He said: And what is in my soul? He said: I strike with my sword before you until Allah grants you victory or I am killed. So he pledged to him, and the people pledged upon the pledge of Abu Sinan. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, nor from Muhammad except Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran; Yaqub ibn Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"2123","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: Mutah was only for us especially, the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning the mutah of hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Shatha except Bayan, nor from Bayan except Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil; Yahya ibn Adam alone transmitted it."
"2124","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Hamdan ibn Umar al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a woman and stood at her middle. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Shababab and Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"2125","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The servant lies until he is written with Allah a liar, and he is truthful until he is written with Allah a siddiq. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Ala except Israil; Abu Ghassan alone transmitted it."
"2126","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Nafi al-Makki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A sheep died in one of the houses of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from its skin. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Nafi except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"2127","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Salamah ibn Nuaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: La ilaha illa Allah enters Paradise, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Shayban."
"2128","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We did not know the hypocrites except by their hatred of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr except Muhammad al-Qasim."
"2129","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated to us, saying: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except al-Masjid al-Haram. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except al-Masudi, nor from al-Masudi except Husayn ibn Muhammad; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi alone transmitted it."
"2130","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to Friday, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid; Zuhayr ibn Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"2131","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Shabbah al-Numayri narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Idris al-Uswari narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated to us, from Yunus al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us extra spoils besides our share of the fifth, and I received an old camel. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki; Ishaq ibn Idris alone transmitted it."
"2132","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Israil, from Abd al-Ala, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Ala except Israil; al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah alone transmitted it."
"2133","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you has a piercing pain in the bowels, let him perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Imran except Muhammad ibn Bilal."
"2134","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Yahya ibn Ubayd Abu Umar al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made obligatory two rakahs in travel, as he made obligatory four in residence. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Ubayd except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal alone transmitted it."
"2135","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ziyad ibn Sad informed me, that Abu Nahik informed him, that Abu al-Darda addressed and said: Whoever is overtaken by dawn has no witr. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be overtaken by dawn and pray witr. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Asim."
"2136","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, saying: Maslamah ibn Alqamah al-Mazini narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral until he prays over it, then leaves, he has a qirat of reward; and if he follows it, prays over it, then sits until its burial is finished, he has two qirats, each of them greater than Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Maslamah ibn Alqamah."
"2137","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Shuayb ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Tahhan al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade confining animals to be shot at. No one narrated this hadith from Salim al-Aftas except Sufyan; Muammal alone transmitted it."
"2138","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: I saw myself scraping semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would pray. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Israil; al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah alone transmitted it."
"2139","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade inciting animals against one another. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash from al-Minhal except Ziyad ibn Abd Allah."
"2140","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has pardoned for this ummah mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd al-Ammi except his son; al-Harashi alone transmitted it."
"2141","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees good in his dream, let him praise Allah and mention it; and whoever sees other than that, let him seek refuge in Allah and not mention it, for it will not harm him. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Said ibn Abd al-Rahman; Sulayman ibn Dawud alone transmitted it."
"2142","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, saying: Dawud al-Muhabbar narrated to us, saying: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant commits a sin, and when he remembers it, what he did grieves him; when Allah looks at him grieved by what he did, He forgives him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Salih al-Murri; Dawud al-Muhabbar alone transmitted it."
"2143","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, saying: Qudamah ibn Shihab al-Mazini narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best earning? He said: The work of a man with his hand, and every righteous sale. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Qudamah; al-Hasan ibn Arafah alone transmitted it."
"2144","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil Yahya ibn Habib ibn Abd Allah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Abd al-Hamid; Abu Aqil alone transmitted it."
"2145","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Zakariyya al-Suraymi narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the overwhelming of debt, from the overwhelming of the enemy, from the ruin of the widow without husband, and from the trial of the Dajjal. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abbad ibn Zakariyya; al-Qulusi alone transmitted it."
"2146","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who strikes cheeks, tears garments, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yazid ibn Harun."
"2147","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubadah ibn al-Walid al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, saying: Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you spit in front of him in prayer, nor to his right, but let him spit to his left."
"2148","And with its chain: from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prostrate spreading his forearms like the dog. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sulaym ibn Hayyan except Habban ibn Hilal."
"2149","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubayd Allah al-Kurayzi narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dreams are from Allah, and confused dreams are from Satan; when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left, and seek refuge from its evil, and it will not harm him. No one narrated it from al-Zuhri from Abu Umamah from Abu Hurayrah except Salih; Abd al-Ghaffar alone transmitted it. And the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Qatadah, and that is the correct version."
"2150","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the fatwa by which the Ansar used to give fatwa, water is from water, was a concession in the beginning of Islam. No one narrated it from al-Zuhri from Ata except Salih. And the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sad, and that is the correct version."
"2151","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hani al-Naysaburi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two are not to converse privately to the exclusion of a third."
"2152","And with its chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man is not to make a man rise from his place and sit in it; when he returns, he has more right to it."
"2153","And with its chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you dozes on Friday, let him move from his place. No one narrated these hadiths from Abu Ishaq except Abu Shihab."
"2154","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Bashir al-Aslami narrated to us, saying: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, from his father, that his uncle Amir ibn al-Akwa was wounded on the day of Khaybar and killed a man, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has two rewards. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bishr except Abu Ahmad."
"2155","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abu Shaybah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Nahhas narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Maqil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man who is in charge of a people, then does not guard them as he guards himself and his family, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will admit him into Hellfire. No one narrated it from Khalid except Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Nahhas."
"2156","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Zayd, give the zakat of your head along with the people, even if you find nothing but a thread."
"2157","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to me, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from his uncle Qutbah ibn Malik, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing so long in voluntary prayer that his feet would swell, and it was said: Do you exert yourself, what is this exertion when Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: Shall I not be a thankful servant. None of those who narrated it from Misar inserted Qutbah between Ziyad ibn Ilaqah and al-Mughirah except Ibn Ishaq."
"2158","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us, from Maruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib addressed, praised Allah and extolled Him, and mentioned the Commander of the Believers Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the seal of the trustees, the trustee of the seal of the prophets, and the trusted one of the truthful and the martyrs. Then he said: O people, a man has parted from you whom neither the first nor the last can catch up with; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give him the banner, and Jibril would fight on his right and Mikail on his left, and he would not return until Allah granted victory through him; Allah took his soul on the night in which the trustee of Musa was taken, his spirit was raised on the night in which the spirit of Isa son of Maryam was raised, and on the night in which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down al-Furqan. By Allah, he left no gold nor silver nor anything hoarded, and in his treasury there was only seven hundred and fifty dirhams left over from his stipend, with which he wanted to buy a servant for Umm Kulthum. Then he said: Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am al-Hasan son of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he recited this verse, the saying of Yusuf: And I followed the religion of my fathers, Ibrahim, Ishaq, and Yaqub. Then he took up the Book of Allah and said: I am the son of the bearer of glad tidings, I am the son of the warner, I am the son of the Prophet, I am the son of the caller to Allah by His permission, I am the son of the luminous lamp, I am the son of the one sent as mercy to the worlds, I am of the People of the House from whom Allah removed impurity and purified thoroughly, and I am of the People of the House whose love and allegiance Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made obligatory, for He said in what He sent down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say: I ask you no reward for it except love for kin. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Tufayl except Maruf ibn Kharrabudh, nor from Maruf except Sallam ibn Abi Amrah; Ismail ibn Aban alone transmitted it."
"2159","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Hisham ibn al-Fadl ibn Dalham al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, from Abu Dawud al-Subayi, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: None loves you except a believer, and none hates you except a hypocrite. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Hasirah except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"2160","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Hisham ibn al-Fadl ibn Dalham al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Hazawwar narrated to us, from Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has adorned you with an adornment with which He has adorned no servant like it: Allah has made beloved to you the poor, and closeness to them, and made you an imam for them whom they approve, and made them followers for you who approve of you; so glad tidings to whoever loves you and is truthful toward you, and woe to whoever hates you and lies against you. As for whoever loves you and is truthful toward you, they are your neighbors in your abode, and your companions in your Paradise; and as for whoever hates you and lies against you, it is incumbent upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to make them stand in the stations of liars. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone transmitted it."
"2161","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: What do you say about two dirhams equated with one good dirham? He said: What harm in that? Is that but like two camels for a fat she-camel? Abu Said al-Khudri said: O Ibn Abbas, are you the one who consumes riba and feeds it to people? He said: Who is this? He said: Abu Said. He said: I did not know that anyone who knows my kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would dare this daring against me. Abu Said said: By Allah, I say that to you only as counsel for you and compassion toward you; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, like for like; dates for dates, like for like; salt for salt, like for like. No one narrated this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"2162","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Mujabbir, from Abu Majid, from Ibn Masud, who said: We asked our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral? He said: Walking with it is less than trotting; if it is good, it is hastened to it, and if it is evil, then away with the companions of the Fire; the funeral is followed and does not follow, and he is not from us who goes ahead of it. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Salih except Amir ibn Mudrik."
"2163","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Matar ibn Tarif, from al-Shabi, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I said to Ali: O Commander of the Believers, do you have of revelation anything except what is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic? He said: No, by the One who split the seed and created the soul, I do not know it, except understanding that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives a man in the Quran, and what is in the leaf. I said: And what is in the leaf? He said: Blood-money, freeing the captive, and that no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Amir ibn Mudrik."
"2164","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Khallad al-Saffar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stay back from prayer because of what so-and-so prolongs for us; I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angrier at anything than his anger at this, and he said: O people, among you are those who repel; whichever of you prays with people, let him lighten, for among them are the small, the old, and the one with need."
"2165","And from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; when you see that, prayer is incumbent upon you."
"2166","And from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, pointing with his hand toward Yemen: Faith is here, and harshness and hardness of heart are among the loud-voiced herdsmen at the rising of the sun, where the horn of Satan rises, at the roots of the tails of camels, in Rabiah and Mudar. No one narrated these hadiths from Khallad al-Saffar except Amir ibn Mudrik."
"2167","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman except Abu Asim."
"2168","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn al-Nadr al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people of Madinah, remember the Day of Deliverance. They said: And what is the Day of Deliverance? He said: The Dajjal will come until he alights at Dhubab, and no male or female polytheist, no male or female disbeliever, no male or female hypocrite, and no male or female sinner will remain in Madinah except that he will go out to him, and the believers will be purified; that is the Day of Deliverance. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Jurayri except Ali ibn Asim."
"2169","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they appoint Abu Bakr as successor, they will find him a submitted, trustworthy one, abstinent in this world, desirous of the Hereafter; and if they appoint Umar as commander, they will find him strong, trustworthy, not seized in Allah by the blame of a blamer; and if they appoint Ali, and I do not think they will do so, they will find him a guiding, guided one, taking them along the straight path. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"2170","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Salim, who said: I heard Abu Said al-Azdi saying: Abd Allah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite seventy surahs before Zayd ibn Thabit became Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Salim except Abu Awanah."
"2171","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Junayd al-Daqqaq narrated to us, saying: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contest except in arrows, hooves, or camels. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, brother of Fulayh; Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna alone transmitted it."
"2172","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the offspring of the Ansar, the offspring of the offspring of the Ansar, and the freedmen of the Ansar. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar except Ali ibn Thabit."
"2173","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that she arrived performing umrah, then menstruated before circumambulating the House, so she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he commanded her to enter ihram for hajj, and when she completed her rites, she said: O Messenger of Allah, my sisters return with hajj and umrah, and I return with hajj? He said: Go out with your brother. So she went out with him to al-Tanim, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at al-Abtah waiting for her, and it became the practice of people. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Fayyad except Israil; Ubayd Allah ibn Musa alone transmitted it."
"2174","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, saying: Musa al-Juhani narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were in a house, took hold of the two doorposts, then said: I have a right upon you, and the imams of Quraysh have, so long as they act by three: if they judge, they are just; if mercy is sought from them, they show mercy; and if they covenant, they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Musa al-Juhani."
"2175","Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Kurdi al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Said ibn Amir."
"2176","2173 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Habban al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Baqiyyah."
"2177","2174 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Yunus ibn Mihran al-Zayyat narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Sulayman al-Aswad, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man came after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already prayed, so he said: Is there no man who will give charity to this one and pray with him? No one placed Khalid al-Hadhdha between Wuhayb and Sulayman al-Aswad among those who narrated this hadith from Wuhayb except Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami."
"2178","2175 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yusuf al-Misli narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ziyad al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the dawn, then pray Witr with one rakah."
"2179","2176 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a person who has a will to make to spend two nights except with his will written down. No one narrated these two hadiths from Khalid ibn Ziyad except Muhammad ibn Abi Yusuf."
"2180","2177 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had thick curly hair reaching the shoulders. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim."
"2181","2178 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Shuayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from his father, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the individual by twenty-five. No one narrated this hadith from Shuayb except his son Abd al-Salam."
"2182","2179 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanabah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Majzaah ibn Zahir, from Ibn Abi Awfa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water, O Allah, purify me of sins as the white garment is purified of filth. No one narrated this hadith from Raqabah except Ibrahim ibn Yazid."
"2183","2180 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Marrudhi narrated to us, he said: Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness never enters into anything except that it beautifies it, and it is never removed from anything except that it disgraces it. No one narrated this hadith from Raqabah except Abu Hamzah."
"2184","2181 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah al-Mismai narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who sleeps while in a state of major ritual impurity. He said: He should perform ablution, then sleep."
"2185","2182 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Sabii Amr ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: al-Aswad ibn Yazid informed me, that Aishah informed him, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his night prayer he prayed Witr, then came to his bed; when the caller to prayer called, he sprang from his bed; if he was in a state of major impurity he poured water over himself, and if he was not, he performed the ablution for prayer, then came and prayed."
"2186","2183 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Khalid Abu Amr al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Qasim al-Kindi narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) holding the hand of Ali while saying: This is my ally and I am his ally; I befriend whoever befriends him, and I oppose whoever opposes him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Wail except al-Mualla ibn Irfan; Ali ibn al-Qasim al-Kindi alone narrated it."
"2187","2184 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the men and women, and he urged the men to give charity, then he turned to the women and urged them to give charity. So Zaynab, the wife of Abd Allah, sent Bilal to him and said: Convey greetings to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a woman among the Emigrants, without naming her, and ask him: Does she earn any reward for spending her charity on her Emigrant husband who has nothing, and on orphans in her care who are her brother's sons? Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Yes, she has two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Shaqiq except al-Masudi; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr alone narrated it."
"2188","2185 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Warqa ibn Umar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount stood upright with him. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Warqa."
"2189","2186 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No soul is killed except that a share of it falls upon the son of Adam, for he was the first to institute killing. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mutamir; Amr ibn Asim alone narrated it. Sulayman differed from the companions of al-Amash in its chain, saying: from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Shaqiq, while al-Thawri and others narrated it from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas."
"2190","2187 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mualla ibn Mansur al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Qazaah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr except Mindal, nor from Mindal except Abu Ghassan; Yahya ibn al-Mualla alone narrated it."
"2191","2188 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave him a sa of food and ordered his family to lighten his burden. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid."
"2192","2189 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Awf al-Arabi, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the Day of Sacrifice: Come, pick up pebbles for me. So I picked up for him pebbles like those of khadhf. He said: With the likes of these, throw; for those before you perished only through extremism in religion. None of those who narrated this hadith from Awf, from Ziyad, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas mentioned: from al-Fadl, except Jafar; Abd al-Razzaq alone narrated it. And people narrated it from Awf, from Ziyad, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas."
"2193","2190 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Dallawayh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise. No one narrated it from Said ibn Masruq except Qays ibn al-Rabi; Ali ibn Thabit alone narrated it."
"2194","2191 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Maruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir, from Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The feet of a servant will not move until he is asked about four things: about his body in what he wore it out, his life in what he spent it, his wealth from where he earned it and in what he spent it, and about love of the People of the House. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the sign of love for you? So he struck with his hand upon the shoulder of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2195","2192 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishkab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Mujahid, from Umm Salamah who said: One of us would menstruate in her garment, and when the day of her purity came she would wash what had touched it, then pray in it; yet today one of you frees her servant to wash her clothes on the day of her purity. No one narrated it from Mujahid except Khalid; al-Minhal alone narrated it."
"2196","2193 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Badr Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Ruhayl ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali who said: Bathing on Friday is recommended, but it is not obligatory. No one narrated it from al-Ruhayl except Shuja."
"2197","2194 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Ziyad al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites this Quran will be with the noble righteous scribes, and whoever stammers in it will have two rewards. No one narrated it from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Isa ibn Shuayb."
"2198","2195 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Anbasah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from al-Musayyab ibn Najabah, from Ali who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The one consulted is entrusted, so when he is consulted let him advise with what he would do for himself. No one narrated it except Abd al-Rahman ibn Anbasah, and it is a strange hadith."
"2199","2196 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muammar ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Zufar narrated to us, from Ismail, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah who said: I entered while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so I bowed outside the row, then walked until I entered the row. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished he said: May Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat. No one narrated it from Zufar except Ibn Mudrik."
"2200","2197 - Ahmad ibn Zakariyya Shadhan al-Qasri narrated to us, he said: Barakah ibn Muhammad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Aishah who said: I never saw the private parts of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at all. No one narrated it except Barakah ibn Muhammad."
"2201","2198 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zaybaqi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani and Abi Yafur, from Ibn Abi Awfa who said: We went on seven campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eating locusts. No one narrated it from al-Shaybani except Abu Awanah, nor from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Hammad; al-Hasan ibn Mudrik alone narrated it."
"2202","2199 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik al-Qasri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, that he said: Abu Hakim al-Dabbi narrated to me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing a servant will be held to account for on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. Allah the Almighty will say to His angels: Look at the prayer of My servant, did he complete it or fall short? If he completed it, it will be recorded for him as complete, and if he fell short, it will be said: Look, does My servant have voluntary prayers to complete his obligation with? Then the rest of the deeds will be taken likewise."
"2203","2200 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds and pitched vessels. No one narrated them from Ibn Thawban except Utbah ibn Hammad."
"2204","2201 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qasri al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Suayr ibn al-Khums, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: Abu Bakr in Paradise, Umar in Paradise, Uthman in Paradise, Ali in Paradise, Talhah in Paradise, al-Zubayr in Paradise, Sad in Paradise, Said in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf in Paradise, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah in Paradise. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Hamid ibn Yahya, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain."
"2205","2202 - Ahmad ibn Wahb Abu Zayd al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam informed us, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah takes away his sight and he is patient and seeks reward, it becomes incumbent upon Allah that his eyes will not see the Fire. No one narrated it except Wahb ibn Hafs."
"2206","2203 - Ahmad ibn al-Khalil al-Jurayri al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard, and he said: A nation that was transformed, and Allah knows best. No one narrated it from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Muhammad ibn Sawa."
"2207","2204 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mabahr am al-Idhaji narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghalib ibn Rashid al-Abshami narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from al-Hasan who said: I heard Muawiyah delivering a sermon saying: One day I poured the ablution water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he raised his head to me and said: You will indeed take charge of the affairs of my nation after me, so when that happens, accept from their righteous and overlook their wrongdoers. He said: I kept hoping for it until I stood in this station of mine. No one narrated it from Ghalib al-Qattan except Yahya ibn Ghalib ibn Rashid."
"2208","2205 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Misri al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Lahiq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who visits the sick wades into mercy, and when he sits with him he plunges into it. No one narrated it from al-Mufaddal except Abu Asim."
"2209","2206 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A person is with whom he loves. No one narrated it from Ismail except Imran ibn Uyaynah."
"2210","2207 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nakhai the judge narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nahdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty says: Allah's anger is severe against whoever wrongs one who finds no helper besides Me. No one narrated it from Abu Ishaq except Sharik; Misar ibn al-Hajjaj alone narrated it."
"2211","2208 - Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn al-Walid al-Sukkari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about lost property. He said: Lost property is not lawful; whoever picks up something must announce it, and if its owner comes let him return it to him, and if he does not come let him give it in charity; then if he comes, let him give him the choice between the reward and what belongs to him. No one narrated it from Ziyad ibn Sad except al-Samti, and no one narrated it from Sumayy except Ziyad ibn Sad."
"2212","2209 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Zafarani al-Askari narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched. No one narrated it from Harun except Abu Qutaybah, and Harun did not narrate with a chain from Yahya any hadith other than this."
"2213","2210 - Ahmad ibn Hammuwayh Abu Sayyar al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abdan al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: When we returned from Tabuk, a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Hour? He said: No hundred years will pass over the people while a single soul alive today remains on the face of the earth. No one narrated it from Dawud, from Abu Uthman, except Ibn Abi Zaidah."
"2214","2211 - Ahmad ibn Hammuwayh Abu Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ayyub narrated to me, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies setting up an equal to Allah, Allah will place him in the Fire. And Abd Allah said: And another that I did not hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which I hope is true: No servant dies without setting up an equal to Allah except that Allah will admit him to Paradise. No one narrated it from Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi except Ibn Abi Zaidah."
"2215","2212 - Ahmad ibn Fadik al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa Abu Ghassan al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: al-Hasan said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a sword, so he gave it to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stipulated to him while the sword was in his hand before handing it to him, saying: Here, O Muhammad, fight the polytheists with it as long as they are fought; then if you see the Muslims fighting each other, take it to Uhud and break it. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except his son."
"2216","2213 - Ahmad ibn Makhlad al-Barathi narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, will we weave our garments in Paradise with our own hands? The people laughed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you laughing at? At an ignorant man asking a learned one? No, O Bedouin, but the fruits of Paradise will split open yielding them. No one narrated it from al-Shabi except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except his son, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"2217","2214 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami, known as Yazid ibn Abi Habib, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Abi Najiyah al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one. None inserted al-Zuhri between Amr ibn Dinar and Ata except Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr."
"2218","2215 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Nubayt ibn Sharit, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: my father Ishaq narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Nubayt ibn Sharit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. It is not narrated from Nubayt except with this chain; his son alone narrated it from him."
"2219","2216 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Burani the judge narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: War is deceit. No one narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ali ibn Ghurab."
"2220","2217 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Burani the judge narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Sudai narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn al-Jarud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Munayyir, the maternal uncle of Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a debtor respite until his ease, Allah the Almighty will grant him respite for his sin until his repentance. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; al-Sudai alone narrated it."
"2221","2218 - Ahmad ibn al-Musayyab ibn Tumah al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah Musab ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands in prayer, let him not close his eyes. It is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain, and no one narrated it from Musa except Musab."
"2222","2219 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Tamimi al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: I was sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came who had performed ablution, but on his foot was a spot the water had not reached. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and complete your ablution, so he did. It is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain."
"2223","2220 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Sulami, at Juniyyah, narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Hisn ibn Hassan al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Preemption applies in every partnership in land or a walled garden; it is not right for him to sell until he informs his partner, who may take it or leave it."
"2224","2221 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearls, in which there is no noise and no toil. No one narrated it from al-Shaybani except Ibn Ayyash, and none narrated it from him except Ibn Abi Saminah."
"2225","2222 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir who said: I said to al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra: Describe the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me. She said: Whenever I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I saw him like the rising sun. This hadith is not narrated from al-Rubayyi except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Musa alone narrated it."
"2226","2223 - Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Saffar al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I never regretted anything as I regretted not asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the wind. Abu Hurayrah said: Indeed I asked him about it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the wind made of? He said: From the mercy of Allah; He sends it with mercy and sends it with punishment. No one narrated it from Shibl except Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa."
"2227","2224 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Tamimi Abu al-Saqr al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You burn, you burn, then when you pray Fajr it washes them away; then you burn, you burn, then when you pray Zuhr it washes them away; then you burn, you burn, then when you pray Asr it washes them away; then you burn, you burn, then when you pray Maghrib it washes them away; then you burn, you burn, then when you pray Isha it washes them away; then you sleep and nothing is recorded against you until you wake. Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi raised it as a prophetic hadith, while a group narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah as a stopped report."
"2228","2225 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzaz al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Miskin Abu Fatimah narrated to us, from Hawshab, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three things: Witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and bathing on Friday."
"2229","2226 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Miskin narrated to us, from Hawshab, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched. No one narrated these two hadiths from Hawshab ibn Aqil except Miskin, and none narrated them from him except Ismail ibn Bishr."
"2230","2227 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Salam al-Jawaliqi al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ibrahim al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Habati narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Hakim narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How excellent a condiment is vinegar."
"2231","2228 - Ahmad ibn Hamdan Abu Said al-Tustari, at Abbadam, narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: We sighted the crescent of Dhu al-Hijjah as a huge moon, the one who minimizes saying it was of two nights and the one who exaggerates saying it was of three. When we arrived at Makkah, I met Ibn Abbas and asked him about the Day of Tarwiyah, and he counted for me from that day. I said: We sighted it as a huge moon. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended it to its sighting. No one narrated it from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb. And Shubah narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah."
"2232","2229 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Thawab al-Husri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: al-Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them and forgot something in the prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud, then gave salutation. No one narrated it except Muhammad ibn Thawab."
"2233","2230 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Murri al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Layth, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to love of us, the People of the House, for whoever meets Allah the Almighty while loving us will enter Paradise through our intercession; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no deed benefits a servant except through recognizing our right."
"2234","2231 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi al-Basri, at Basrah, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid eating leeks and onions."
"2235","2232 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Qarqarah al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Sayyar al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the son of Adam died, Adam said to his wife Hawwa: Your son has died. She said: What is death? He said: He neither eats, nor drinks, nor walks, nor grasps. When he said that, she screamed. He said: Wailing is upon you and your daughters, while I and my sons are innocent of it; so lamentations became the practice of women. It is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah except with this chain."
"2236","2233 - Ahmad ibn Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Jabbarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah who said: A man came to Abu Musa and said: A man died leaving his daughter, his son's daughter, and a sister. He said: For the daughter is half, and for the sister is half, and you will go to Ibn Masud and he will say the same to you. So I went to Ibn Masud and said: Abu Musa told me such and such. Ibn Masud said: I would have strayed then and would not be among the guided: for the daughter is half, for the son's daughter the completion, and for the sister the third; thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportion it. No one narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah except Qays, nor from Abu Ubaydah except Amr ibn Murrah."
"2237","2234 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Harun ibn Sulayman ibn Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Shuayb al-Himmani narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at Zahr Marr, and a limb of game was gifted to him, so he returned it to the messenger and said to him: Convey greetings to him and say: Were we not in ihram we would not have returned it to you."
"2238","2235 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mirdas al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samurah al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you even find two garments? No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except al-Muharibi."
"2239","2236 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Makhshi, the nephew of al-Makhshi al-Farghani, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: my maternal uncle al-Mughirah ibn al-Hasan ibn Rashid al-Hashimi narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how much he prayed; so when one of you finds that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"2240","2237 - And from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I brought my son, who had not yet eaten food, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he placed him in his lap, and he urinated on the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called for water and sprinkled it over his garment, and did not wash it."
"2241","2238 - And from Ibn Shihab, that he heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, let him sniff water into his nose, and whoever cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"2242","2239 - And from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abd Allah ibn Zayd, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclining in the mosque with one of his feet placed over the other."
"2243","2240 - And from Ibn Shihab, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him, that Aishah used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No calamity befalls a Muslim except that it expiates for him, even the thorn he is pricked with."
"2244","2241 - And from Ibn Shihab, that Urwah informed him, that Aishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gecko is a harmful little creature."
"2245","2242 - And from Ibn Shihab, that Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf informed him, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl informed him, that Said ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wrongfully takes anything of land will be encircled with it from seven earths."
"2246","2243 - And from Ibn Shihab, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Qays al-Ansari, that Thabit ibn Qays said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared that I may have perished. He said: Why? He said: I find myself loving pride, and Allah the Almighty forbids us to raise our voices above your voice, while I am loud-voiced. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?"
"2247","2244 - And from Ibn Shihab, that Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali and Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed him, that their father Muhammad ibn Ali informed them, that he heard Ali say to Ibn Abbas: You are a confused man; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women on the day of Khaybar, and eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"2248","2245 - And from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, that Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to him, that al-Sab ibn Jaththamah ibn Qays narrated to him, that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild donkey while he was at Waddan or at al-Abwa, and he returned it to him. He said: He recognized distress at his returning it on my face, so he said: It is not our returning it to you, but we are in ihram."
"2249","2246 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Akhi al-Makhshi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: my maternal uncle al-Mughirah ibn al-Hasan ibn Rashid al-Hashimi narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar who said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: Woe to you, what is wrong with you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife while fasting in Ramadan. He said: Can you find a slave to free? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Can you fast two consecutive months? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Can you feed sixty poor persons? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. So he turned away from him. While they were thus, a basket containing dates was brought. He said: Where is the one who came? He was called for him, and he said: Take this and give it in charity. He said: Upon any poorer than my family, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, between its two lava plains there is no household poorer than us. He laughed until his eyeteeth appeared, then said: Take it and feed your family with it. These hadiths are not narrated from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except with this chain; Ubayd Allah ibn Said ibn Ufayr alone narrated them."
"2250","2247 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Kaysan who said: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas who said: Abu Bakr went out at midday, and Umar heard of it, so he went out and there was Abu Bakr. He said: O Abu Bakr, what brought you out at this hour? He said: By Allah, I find in my stomach the grip of hunger. He said: And I, by Allah, nothing brought me out but it. While they were thus, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them and said: What brought you two out at this hour? They said: By Allah, what we find in our stomachs of the grip of hunger brought us out. He said: And I, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing brought me out but it, so stand. They stood and went until they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Abu Ayyub used to store for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) food or milk, but that day he was late and did not come at its time, so his family fed it to him, and he went to his palm trees working in them. When they came to the door of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, a woman came out and said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and those with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Where is Abu Ayyub? She said: He will come to you, O Prophet of Allah, presently. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, and Abu Ayyub saw him while working in his palms, so he came hurrying until he caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Welcome to the Prophet of Allah and those with him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is not the time you used to come to me. He turned him back, then went to a cluster of the palm and cut it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What did you intend by this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I wished that you eat of its fresh ripe dates, its unripe dates, and its dried dates, and I shall also slaughter for you with it. He said: If you slaughter, do not slaughter one with milk. So he took a young goat of his and slaughtered it, and said to his wife: Bake, and I shall cook, for you know baking best. He took half the kid and cooked it, and roasted half of it. When the food was ready it was placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took some of the kid and placed it upon a loaf and said: O Abu Ayyub, convey this to Fatimah, for she has not had the like of this for days. When they ate and were satisfied, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bread and meat and unripe dates and dried dates and fresh dates, and his eyes filled with tears, then he said: This is the bliss you will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection. That weighed heavily upon his companions, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you obtain the like of this and strike with your hands, say: In the name of Allah and by the blessing of Allah; and when you are satisfied, say: Praise be to Allah who has fed us to fullness, quenched us, blessed us and favored us; for this suffices for that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never have a kindness done to him by anyone except that he loved to repay him, so he said to Abu Ayyub: Come to us tomorrow. He did not hear, so Umar said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders you to come to him. When he came to him, he gave him a slave girl and said: O Abu Ayyub, treat her well, for we have seen nothing but good as long as she was with us. When Abu Ayyub brought her, he said: I find nothing better for the instruction of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than to free her, so he freed her. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Kaysan except al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"2251","2248 - Ahmad ibn Amr Abu Talhah al-Mujashii al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hilw ibn al-Sari al-Awdi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not find one of you placing one of his feet over the other, then singing and neglecting to recite Surah al-Baqarah. No one narrated this hadith from Hilw ibn al-Sari except al-Harith ibn Muhammad; Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi alone narrated it."
"2252","2249 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jawaribi al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle Ali ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man may be the protector of the people and defend his companions; will his share be like the share of others? He said: May your mother mourn you; are you provided and helped except through your weak ones? No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar; Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"2253","2250 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, he said: my uncle Ali ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray leaning toward a tree trunk; a Byzantine man passed and said: If Muhammad called me I would make for him something more comfortable than this. She said: He was called for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he made for him a pulpit of four steps. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon, and the trunk moaned as the she-camel moans. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended to it and said: What is the matter with you? If you wish I shall call upon Allah and He will return you to your enclosure, and if you wish I shall call upon Allah and Allah will admit you to Paradise, so you will bear fruit therein and the sent prophets of Allah and His righteous servants will eat of your fruit. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Yes. Then the trunk sank and was gone. No one narrated this hadith from Aishah except Ibn Buraydah, nor from Ibn Buraydah except Salih ibn Hayyan, nor from Salih except Hibban, nor from Hibban except Qabisah; Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi alone narrated it."
"2254","2251 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever man calls another man an unbeliever, then if he is an unbeliever, otherwise it returns with unbelief upon him. Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah did not narrate from Nafi any hadith other than this, and none narrated it from Abd al-Aziz except his son, nor from his son except Hashim ibn Abd al-Wahid."
"2255","2252 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mahdhurah Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a sound before me; it was said: This is Bilal. And I saw Umm Sulaym bint Milhan in Paradise."
"2256","2253 - Ahmad ibn Yahya Thalab the grammarian narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah ibn Abi al-Ruqad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Atiyyah: When you circumcise, leave some and do not cut deeply, for it is brighter for the face and more pleasing to the husband. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Thabit, nor from Thabit except Zaidah ibn Abi al-Ruqad; Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi alone narrated it."
"2257","2254 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Kaysan al-Thaqafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Umayrah ibn Sad who said: I witnessed Ali on the pulpit adjuring the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm say what he said, let him testify. Twelve men stood, among them Abu Said, Abu Hurayrah, and Anas ibn Malik, and they testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Ismail ibn Amr."
"2258","2255 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Kaysan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obedience to Allah is obedience to the father, and disobedience to Allah is disobedience to the father. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth ibn Sad except Ismail ibn Amr, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"2259","2256 - Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari and Abi Tuwalah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The superiority of Aishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over all other food. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Ismail ibn Ayyash; Yahya ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"2260","2257 - Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter. When the Day of Resurrection comes, every Muslim man will be given a man of the Jews and Christians, and it will be said: O Muslim, this is your ransom from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr except Jafar ibn al-Harith, nor from Jafar al-Harith except Ismail; Yahya ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"2261","2258 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Baladi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Aishah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, that his grandfather Umayr ibn Habib ibn Khumashah, who had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his puberty, advised his son saying: O my son, beware of sitting with fools, for sitting with them is a disease; whoever forbears toward the fool is gladdened, whoever answers him regrets, whoever is not content with little of what the fool brings will be content with much; and when one of you wishes to enjoin good or forbid evil, let him prepare himself to bear harm patiently and trust in reward from Allah the Almighty, for whoever trusts in reward from Allah will not be harmed by the touch of harm. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi except Hammad ibn Salamah; Ibn Aishah alone narrated it."
"2262","2259 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Baladi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aishah narrated to us, he said: Durayd ibn Mujashi narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from Malik ibn Dinar, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: O Ahnaf, whoever laughs much loses dignity; whoever jokes is taken lightly; whoever does much of a thing is known by it; whoever speaks much errs much; whoever errs much loses modesty; whoever loses modesty loses piety; and whoever loses piety, his heart dies. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ibn Aishah alone narrated it."
"2263","2260 - Ahmad ibn Mujahid al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Tumah ibn Amr al-Jafari, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: I came to Umm Salamah to console her for al-Husayn ibn Ali. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and sat upon a sleeping mat of hers; Fatimah came with a skin vessel and placed it. He said: Call Hasan and Husayn and your cousin Ali. When they gathered with him, he said: O Allah, these are my elite and my Household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. No one narrated this hadith from Tumah ibn Amr except Zafir ibn Sulayman; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"2264","2261 - Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cutting is for a quarter of a dinar. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani except his son Hisham."
"2265","2262 - Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Khalil al-Khushani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prayer except with the Opening of the Book, and two verses with it. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz except al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani."
"2266","2263 - Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Irak ibn Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh, from Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was consoled for his daughter Ruqayyah, the wife of Uthman ibn Affan, he said: Praise be to Allah; burying daughters is among noble deeds. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan al-Dimashqi alone narrated it."
"2267","2264 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qahir narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Khaybari al-Lakhmi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Said narrated to me, he said: Amir al-Shabi narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between the lawful and the unlawful are doubtful matters; many people do not know whether they are of the lawful or of the unlawful. The one who leaves them guards his honor and religion more strictly, and whoever falls into them is likely to fall into the unlawful, like one who grazes beside a sanctuary and is likely to graze within it. Indeed every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except Munabbih ibn Uthman and al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"2268","2265 - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Simt, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Salman, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, then turned a cloak over him and wiped his face with it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except Yazid ibn al-Simt; Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari alone narrated it."
"2269","2266 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that he sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Who is it? He said: It is I. He said: I, I! As though he disliked it."
"2270","2267 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bint Shurahbil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who has a wet dream: Must she bathe? He said: Yes, if she finds water let her bathe."
"2271","2268 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr who said: Two Bedouins came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: Who are the best of people, O Muhammad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lives long and does good deeds. The other said: The laws of Islam have become many for us, so which shall we hold to? He said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Hassan ibn Nuh except Ali ibn Ayyash."
"2272","2269 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A time will come upon people when whoever does not have yellow and white with him will not enjoy life. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam except Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid; Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Irq alone narrated it."
"2273","2270 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Damiri al-Misri, at Damirah, narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Duwayd ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath ibn Qays al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No wealth decreases through charity, and no man pardons a wrong except that Allah increases him in honor through it, so pardon and Allah will honor you; and no man opens upon himself a door of begging except that Allah opens upon him a door of poverty. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi and Zakariyya ibn Duwayd al-Ashathi."
"2274","2271 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Yazid ibn al-Akhnas, who had companionship, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no rivalry among you except in two things: a man to whom Allah the Almighty has given the Quran, so he stands with it night and day following what is in it, and a man says: If only Allah had given me like what He gave so-and-so, I would stand with it as he stands. And a man to whom He has given wealth, so he spends and gives charity, and a man says the like of that. Yazid ibn al-Akhnas did not narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) any hadith other than this; Zayd ibn Waqid alone narrated it."
"2275","2272 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Banna al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar bequeathed the land of Khaybar for the poor, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Keep its principal and give its yield in charity; and it continues upon that to this day. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, and Abu Dawud al-Hafari."
"2276","2273 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Yazdad al-Tabarani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ismah al-Nasibi narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Hakim, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The passing of my nation is through stabbing and plague. We said: We know stabbing, but what is plague? He said: The piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and in each is martyrdom. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, nor from Ibrahim except Bishr ibn Hakim, nor from Bishr except Abd Allah ibn Ismah; Musa ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"2277","2274 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Sad al-Murri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Said al-Suri narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah, al-Amash, and Mansur narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban who said: When: And those who hoard gold and silver was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to gold and silver. They said: What wealth shall we take? He said: A grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Murrah, except Muammal, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Muzani al-Wasiti, and Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad."
"2278","2275 - Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Rawh al-Bardhai narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, originated and made, and from every harmful eye. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, except al-Firyabi. And people narrated it from Sufyan, from Mansur, from al-Minhal."
"2279","2276 - Ahmad ibn Shahin al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: Those who are heedless of their prayer? He said: They are those who delay it beyond its time. None raised this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim."
"2280","2277 - Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Wasawisi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was purifying himself, with a vessel before him of about a mudd, and if it exceeded, it hardly exceeded, and if it lessened, it hardly lessened. He washed his hands, rinsed his mouth and nose three times each, washed his face three times, ran his fingers through his beard, washed his forearms three times each, wiped his head and ears twice each, and washed his feet until he cleaned them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this the purification? He said: Thus did my Lord the Almighty command me. None narrated this wording about running fingers through the beard in ablution from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except Nafi Abu Hurmuz; Shayban alone narrated it."
"2281","2278 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Aqta al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihrqani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Qirat narrated to us, from Jasr Abu Jafar, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A person is with whom he loves. No one narrated it from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Jasr Abu Jafar and Abu Umarah al-Razi."
"2282","2279 - Ahmad ibn al-Khattab al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah al-Sakhtiyani, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the oft-repentant is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Hasan ibn Dinar; Muhammad ibn Ishaq alone narrated it."
"2283","2280 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Sawti Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Nubayt narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am Ahmad, and Muhammad, and the Gatherer, and the Follower, and the Seal. No one narrated it from al-Dahhak except Salamah ibn Nubayt; Abu Nuaym alone narrated it."
"2284","2281 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb and Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mushash, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us wrapped in a cotton garment, with a short spear in his hand, leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd; he fixed it before him, then prayed toward it. No one narrated this hadith from Mushash except Shubah, and none narrated from Mushash anyone other than Shubah."
"2285","2282 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Jawhari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Zabbar al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Sharqi ibn al-Qutami narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Talq al-Aidhi narrating from Shurahbil ibn al-Qaqa, from Amr ibn Madi Karib al-Zubaydi who said: You have seen us from near, when we performed pilgrimage we would say: Labbayk wara, and you have seen us standing at the valley of Muhassir fearing the jinn would snatch us away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Move away from the valley of Uranah, for they are your brothers when they embraced Islam. And he taught us the talbiyah: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; Labbayk, there is no partner for You, Labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. No one narrated this hadith from Sharqi ibn al-Qutami except Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Zabbar al-Kalbi."
"2286","2283 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Zabbar al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from Aishah bint Sad, from her father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will be trials in which a man wakes a believer and sleeps an unbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes an unbeliever. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, which man is most guided? He said: A man between these two sanctuaries in a small group, establishing prayer at its times, performing Hajj and Umrah, remaining thus until a mistaken hand or a decreed death comes to him. No one narrated this hadith from Aishah bint Sad except Salih ibn Abd al-Rahman; Muhammad ibn Ziyad alone narrated it."
"2287","2284 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghazziyah Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father who said: al-Zubayr met a thief and interceded for him. It was said to him: Until we bring him to the ruler. He said: When he reaches the ruler, may Allah curse the intercessor and the one interceded for, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"2288","2285 - Ahmad ibn Umayr ibn Jawsa al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Warqa ibn Umar and Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Baqiyyah; Abu Taqi alone narrated it."
"2289","2286 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghiyath al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sadi al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Yahya al-Muallim al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib came out to us in intense heat wearing winter clothes, and came out to us in winter wearing summer clothes. Then he called for water and drank it, then wiped sweat from his forehead, then returned to his house. I said to my father: O father, did you not see what the Commander of the Faithful did? He came out to us in winter wearing summer clothes, and came out to us in summer wearing winter clothes. Abu Layla said: I did not notice. He took his father's hand and came to Ali and told him what he had done. Ali said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent me while my eyes were sore, and he spat into my eyes, then said: Open your eyes. I opened them, and I have not complained of them to this hour. And he supplicated for me, saying: O Allah, remove from him heat and cold. So I have felt neither heat nor cold to this day of mine. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Ibrahim, and it is not narrated from Ibrahim except with this chain."
"2290","2287 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Sakan ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: I prayed beside Ibrahim al-Saigh wearing a fur, and I was shielding myself with it from the dust. When Ibrahim finished praying, he said to me: Ata said: Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones, and not to gather hair or garment. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, except Ibrahim."
"2291","2288 - Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Haytham al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Fahd ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-some or twenty-five. No one narrated it from Shubah except Fahd."
"2292","2289 - Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, from Sad al-Iskaf, from al-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said: Tamim al-Dari narrated to me that he boarded the sea with some of his family, and the wind drove them to an island in the sea, where they met a densely-haired beast. They said: What are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. Then he mentioned the hadith of al-Jassasah."
"2293","2290 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Sukkari al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge he knows and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Hammad; Muhammad ibn Khulayd alone narrated it."
"2294","2291 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Rajjani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it; and if it is obscured for you, complete the count as thirty. No one narrated it from Warqa except al-Muqri; his son alone narrated it from him."
"2295","2292 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shairi al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam al-Hibri al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, no prayer for one who has no purification, and no religion for one who has no prayer; the place of prayer in religion is like the place of the head in the body. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Mindal, nor from Mindal except Hasan; al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam alone narrated it."
"2296","2293 - Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Subayh al-Madini al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, raisins for raisins, and salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand; whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury. No one narrated this hadith from al-Marur except al-Zubayr; Bishr alone narrated it."
"2297","2294 - The chapter of those whose name is Ibrahim. Ibrahim ibn Abi Sufyan al-Qaysarani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty; and if He were to hold me for what these have earned, He would destroy me. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Firyabi."
"2298","2295 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Firyabi."
"2299","2296 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No son of Adam has done a deed more saving for him from punishment than the remembrance of Allah. It was said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Abu Khalid; al-Firyabi alone narrated it."
"2300","2297 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Fudayk ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ul layy narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us while we were sitting and said: The first of you to meet me at the Basin will be the longest of you in hand. So we began measuring our forearms to see which of us was longest in hand. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not what I mean; I mean the most skillful of you in hand. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Maslamah; Fudayk ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"2301","2298 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Fudayk ibn Sulayman ibn Isa al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salih ibn Bashir ibn Fudayk, who said: Fudayk went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim that whoever does not emigrate perishes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Fudayk, establish prayer, give zakat, abandon evil, and dwell wherever you wish of the land of your people. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Fudayk ibn Sulayman, and Fudayk heard this hadith from al-Awzai."
"2302","2299 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar who said: I acquired land at Khaybar, no wealth dearer to me than it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have acquired land at Khaybar, no wealth more beloved to me than it, and I wish to give it in charity. He said: Keep its principal and give its fruit in charity."
"2303","2300 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Who is Shubrumah? He said: A man who ordered me to perform Hajj on his behalf. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."
"2304","2301 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders; they are asked and give verdicts without knowledge, so they stray and lead astray."
"2305","2302 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibn Masadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr and gave salutation after two rakahs. Dhu al-Yadayn said: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What does Dhu al-Yadayn say? They said: He is right. So he completed the two rakahs with them, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting after giving salutation. Ibn Masadah's name is Abd Allah, among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Razzaq; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah alone narrated it."
"2306","2303 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar Abd Allah ibn Sakhbarah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with three hundred and sixty idols around the Kabah; he began striking them so they fell upon their faces, while saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri except Abd al-Razzaq."
"2307","2304 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri informed us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Masud, from his father who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he passed by a village of ants that had been burned. He said: It is not proper for anyone to punish with the punishment of Allah the Almighty. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri except Abd al-Razzaq."
"2308","2305 - Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Hisham ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
"2309","2306 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar informed us, from Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to a waterskin of theirs, bent its mouth and drank while standing. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Unays except with this chain; Abd al-Razzaq alone narrated it."
"2310","2307 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Bahir the storyteller mention, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from al-Numan ibn Bashir al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate about al-Raqim: Three men entered a cave, and a piece of the mountain fell upon the mouth of the cave and sealed them in. One of them said: O people, recall which of you did a good deed, that Allah in His mercy may have mercy on us. One of them said: I once did a good deed: I had workers I hired for work of mine, each man for a known wage. One day a man came to me in the middle of the day, and I hired him for the rest of the day on the terms of his companions. He worked in the rest of his day as one of them worked in his whole day, so I saw it as a duty not to deduct for him anything of what I had hired his companions for, because of his exertion in his work. One of them said to me: Do you give this one like what you gave me, though he worked only half a day? I said: O servant of Allah, I did not short you anything of your terms; it is only my wealth, I dispose of it as I wish. He became angry at that, left his wage, and I placed his right in a corner of the house as long as Allah willed. Then cattle passed by me, and I bought with it a young calf, kept it until it grew, then sold it, then spent its price on a cow; it became pregnant and multiplied until it reached what Allah willed. Then after a while a weak old man I did not recognize passed by me and said to me: I have a right with you. He mentioned it until I recognized him. I said: Yes, it is you I seek. I offered all of it to him and said: This is your right. He said: O servant of Allah, do not mock me; if you will not give me charity, give me my right. I said: By Allah, I am not jesting with you; it is indeed your right, I have nothing of it. So I handed it to him. O Allah, if I did that for Your sake, relieve us. Then the opening widened until they saw and could see. The second said: I once did a good deed: I had surplus, and hardship befell people. A woman came to me seeking a favor from me. I said to her: No, by Allah, it is not without your giving yourself. She refused me, then returned and reminded me of Allah, but I refused her. I said: No, by Allah, it is not without your giving yourself. She refused me, then mentioned that to her husband, and he said to her: Give him yourself and enrich your dependents. She came to me and adjured me by Allah. I said to her: No, by Allah, it is not without your giving yourself. When she saw that, she submitted herself to me. When I uncovered her and was about to take her, she trembled beneath me. I said: What is wrong with you? She said: I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds. I said to her: You feared Allah in hardship, while I did not fear Him in ease. So I left her and gave her what was due from me for having uncovered her. O Allah, if I did that for Your sake, relieve us. Then the mountain split until they recognized and it became clear to them. The third said: I once did a good deed: I had two aged parents, and I had sheep; I would feed my parents and give them drink, then return to my sheep. One day rain befell me and detained me, and I did not return until evening. I came to my family, took my milking vessel and milked, leaving my sheep standing, and went to my parents to give them drink, but found them asleep. It distressed me to wake them, and distressed me to leave my sheep, so I remained sitting with my milking vessel in my hand until morning woke them. O Allah, if You know I did that for Your sake, relieve us. Al-Numan said: It is as though I hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Then the mountain said: Crack, and Allah relieved them, and they went out."
"2311","2308 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Asim, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2312","2309 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, who said: I entered upon Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah and found him in good spirits. I said: O Abu al-Tufayl, inform me who are the group whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed? He was about to inform me, but his wife Sawdah said: Hush, O Abu al-Tufayl, has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever servant among the believers I supplicate against with a supplication, make it for him purification and mercy. This hadith is not narrated from Sawdah, the wife of Abu al-Tufayl, except with this chain; Umar ibn Habib al-Makki alone narrated it."
"2313","2310 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mamar, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I wish to strive. He said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then strive in them. No one narrated this hadith from Habib, from Ibn Umar, except Mamar; Rabah alone narrated it. And Misar, Sufyan al-Thawri, and others narrated it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abi al-Abbas the poet, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2314","2311 - And with it, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Khirash, from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar, from Mansur, except Rabah. And Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2315","2312 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abi al-Jarrah, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from reciting while I am in a state of major impurity, and forbade me - and I do not say he forbade you - from wearing saffron-dyed clothes, from purple saddle blankets, from wearing a gold ring, and from wearing qassi garments."
"2316","2313 - And with it, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: My soul has become wicked; but let him say: My soul is heavy. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Numan except Abu al-Jarrah; Rabah alone narrated them."
"2317","2314 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, from her mother Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard disputants at his door, so he went out to them and said: I am only a human, and a disputant comes to me, and perhaps one of them is more eloquent in his argument than another, so I judge for him thinking he is truthful; so whoever I judge for him the right of a Muslim, it is only a piece of the Fire, so let him take it or leave it."
"2318","2315 - And with it, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not proper for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. So he attributed him to his father."
"2319","2316 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Walid al-Makhzumi, the imam of the mosque of Sana, narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir, the freedman of the Ansar, informed us, from his uncle, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered with Mariyah the Copt, his concubine, into the house of Hafsah bint Umar, and she found her with him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, in my house apart from the houses of your wives? He said: She is forbidden for me to touch, O Hafsah, and conceal this from me. She went out until she came to Aishah and said: O daughter of Abu Bakr, shall I not give you glad tidings? She said: Of what? She said: I found Mariyah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in my house, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, in my house apart from the houses of your wives? And with me you do this apart from your wives? The first joy was that he forbade her to himself. Then he said to me: O Hafsah, shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. So he informed me that your father will take charge of affairs after him, and that my father will follow after your father, and he asked me to conceal that, so conceal it. Then Allah the Almighty revealed concerning that: O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you - meaning Mariyah - seeking the pleasure of your wives - meaning Hafsah - and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful - meaning for what was from you - Allah has ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths, and Allah is your Protector, and He is the Knowing, the Wise. And when the Prophet confided to one of his wives a statement - meaning Hafsah - then when she informed of it - meaning Aishah - and Allah showed it to him - meaning through the Quran - he made known part of it - he informed Hafsah of what she had disclosed of the matter of Mariyah - and turned aside from part - from what she had informed of the matter of Abu Bakr and Umar, and did not reproach her for it - then when he informed her of it she said: Who informed you of this? He said: The Knowing, the Aware informed me. Then he turned to her reproaching her, saying: If you two turn to Allah, then your hearts have inclined; but if you support one another against him, then Allah is his Protector, and Jibril, and the righteous of the believers - meaning Abu Bakr and Umar - and the angels after that are supporters. Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him wives better than you, submitting, believing, obedient, repentant, worshipping, traveling, previously married and virgins. So He promised him among the previously married: Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, and the sister of Nuh, and among the virgins: Maryam bint Imran, and the sister of Musa, peace be upon them. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"2320","2317 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj al-Basri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wonder at the believer and his distress at sickness; if he knew what is for him in sickness he would love to be sick forever. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the sky and laughed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you raise your head to the sky and laugh? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wondered at two angels who were seeking a servant in a place of prayer he used to be in, but did not find him. They returned and said: O our Lord, Your servant so-and-so, we used to record for him in his day and night the deeds he used to do, but we found him held in Your bonds. Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Record for My servant the deeds he used to do in his day and night, and do not diminish anything of them; upon Me is the reward of what I have confined him with, and for him is the reward of what he used to do. This hadith is not narrated from Utbah ibn Masud except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd alone narrated it."
"2321","2318 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Walid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abd al-Quddus ibn Habib, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O boy, shall I not grant you a gift? Shall I not bestow upon you? Shall I not give you? He said: I said: Yes indeed, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So I thought he would set aside for me a portion of wealth, but he said: Four rakahs which you pray every day; if you cannot then every Friday; if you cannot then every month; if you cannot then every year; if you cannot then once in your lifetime: you say takbir, then recite the Mother of the Quran and a surah, then say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, fifteen times, then you bow and say it ten times, then you rise and say it ten times, then you prostrate and say it ten times, then you rise and say it ten times, then you prostrate and say it ten times, then you rise and say it ten times, then you do likewise in all of your prayer. When you finish, say after the tashahhud and before the taslim: O Allah, I ask You for the success of the people of guidance, the deeds of the people of certainty, the sincere counsel of the people of repentance, the resolve of the patient, the earnestness of the dutiful, the aspiration of the desirous, the worship of the pious, and the knowledge of the learned, until I fear You. O Allah, I ask You for a fear that restrains me from disobeying You, until I work in obedience to You a deed by which I deserve Your pleasure, until I am sincere to You in repentance out of fear of You, until I am sincere to You in counsel out of love for You, until I trust in You in all matters with good expectation of You. Glory be to the Creator of the Fire. If you do that, O Ibn Abbas, Allah will forgive your sins, minor and major, old and new, secret and open, intentional and mistaken. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Abd al-Quddus, nor from Abd al-Quddus except Musa ibn Jafar; Abu al-Walid al-Makhzumi is alone in transmitting it."
"2322","2319 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that it was said to him: We see you wearing Sibti sandals, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing them. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Kathir except Muslim; Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"2323","2320 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu Sinan Isa ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, then two men stepped forward to him: a man from the Ansar and a man from Thaqif, and the Ansari outpaced the Thaqafi. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Thaqafi: The Ansari has preceded you in asking. The Ansari said: Perhaps, O Messenger of Allah, he was more hasty than me, so he is absolved. He said: The Thaqafi asked him about prayer and he informed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Ansari: If you wish I will tell you what you came to ask about, and if you wish you may ask me and I will inform you of that. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you tell me. He said: You came to ask me what reward is yours when you head for the Ancient House, what reward is yours in your standing at Arafah, what reward is yours in your stoning of the Jamarat, what reward is yours in shaving your head, and what reward is yours when you bid farewell to the House. The Ansari said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I came to ask you about nothing else. He said: Your reward when you head for the Ancient House is that neither you nor your mount lifts a foot nor sets it down except that a good deed is written for you and a rank is raised for you. As for your standing at Arafah, Allah Almighty says to His angels: O My angels, what has brought My servants? They say: They have come seeking Your pleasure and Paradise. So Allah Almighty says: I call Myself and My creation to witness that I have forgiven them, as many as the days of eternity, as many as the raindrops, and as many as the sands of Alij. As for your stoning of the Jamarat, Allah Almighty says: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes as reward for what they used to do. As for your shaving your head, there is not a hair of yours that falls to the ground except that it will be a light for you on the Day of Resurrection. As for the House, when you bid it farewell, you emerge from your sins as on the day your mother bore you. This hadith is not narrated from Ubadah except with this chain; Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj is alone in transmitting it."
"2324","2321 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Salim ibn Ju'shum al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir al-Harrani narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi who said: I said to Ibn Umar: When you head toward Makkah you pray upon your mount, so why do you do that? He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it, I would not have done it. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab ibn Bashir; Ibn Ju'shum is alone in transmitting it."
"2325","2322 - And with the same chain: from Khusayf, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the people of Makkah said: The companions of Muhammad are hungry and emaciated, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to trot briskly to show them that they had strength. They would trot briskly for three circuits and walk four. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab."
"2326","2323 - And with the same chain from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that Muawiyah circumambulated the House and began touching all the corners, so Ibn Abbas said to him: Why do you touch these two corners when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not touch them? Muawiyah said: Nothing of the House is to be abandoned. So Ibn Abbas said: You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example. Muawiyah said: You have spoken the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab."
"2327","2324 - And with the same chain from Mujahid, from Aishah, that she said to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief, I would have demolished the House and added to it what was omitted from it, and I would have placed it upon the ground and made for it two doors: a door to enter by and a door to exit by, so that there would be no crowding. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab."
"2328","2325 - And with the same chain from Khusayf, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight."
"2329","2326 - And from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while upon the pulpit, forbidding gold for gold and silver for silver except weight for weight."
"2330","2327 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Sharus narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Aslami narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Arafah at Arafat. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan except Ibrahim."
"2331","2328 - Ibrahim ibn Mamar al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu Qurrah."
"2332","2329 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Samit ibn Muadh al-Janadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is asked by his neighbor to fix a timber in his wall, let him not refuse him."
"2333","2330 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the prostitute and the stud fee of the stallion."
"2334","2331 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale involving uncertainty."
"2335","2332 - And with the same chain the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he fornicates while he is a believer, the thief does not steal while he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine while he drinks it while he is a believer."
"2336","2333 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon sighting it and break fast upon sighting it, and if it is obscured from you then complete the month as thirty."
"2337","2334 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hear the crying of the infant behind me while I am in prayer, so I shorten my prayer out of fear that his mother may be distressed. No one narrated these hadiths from Yaqub except Zam'ah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting them."
"2338","2335 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Humah narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih mentioned, from Abbad ibn Kathir al-Basri, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Miqsam, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The habitual drinker of wine will not enter Paradise, nor one who reminds Allah of his deed as a favor, nor one disobedient to his parents. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Abbad, nor from Abbad except Zam'ah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it. Sufyan narrated it from Mansur, from Salim, from Jaban, from Abd Allah ibn Amr; and Shu'bah narrated it from Mansur, from Salim, from Nubayt ibn Sharit, from Jaban, from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2339","2336 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Humah narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj mentioned: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali informed me, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr except Ibn Jurayj."
"2340","2337 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed eight together and seven together, resident and not on a journey. I said: Where was that? He said: In Madinah. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar except Qays."
"2341","2338 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Hudhayfah who said: The safeguarded ones among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that Ibn Umm Abd is among the nearest of them to Allah in means. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muammal."
"2342","2339 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Jublani narrated to us, he said: al-Yaman ibn Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever unjustly strips the back of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ziyad except al-Yaman."
"2343","2340 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Sulayman al-Shayzari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim, from Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed is he who controls his tongue, whose house suffices him, and who weeps over his sin. This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"2344","2341 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaps his slave unjustly, its expiation is to free him. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Ishaq."
"2345","2342 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever marries a woman for her prestige, Allah will increase him only in humiliation; whoever marries her for her wealth, Allah will increase him only in poverty; whoever marries her for her lineage, Allah will increase him only in baseness; and whoever marries a woman marrying her only to lower his gaze or guard his chastity or join kinship, Allah will bless her for him and bless him for her. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Abd al-Salam."
"2346","2343 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Nusayr al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at those below you and do not look at those above you, for it is more fitting that you not belittle the blessing of Allah Almighty. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Waki; Abd Allah ibn Nusayr is alone in transmitting it."
"2347","2344 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Sindi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to eat horse meat and forbade us donkey meat. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Yusuf."
"2348","2345 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awsabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubaydah al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordering us to bathe on Friday while upon the pulpit."
"2349","2346 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Ayyar narrated to me, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: Some Bedouin Arabs would bring us meat and we felt uneasy about it, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Make them swear firmly that they slaughtered it, then mention the name of Allah and eat. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn al-Ayyar except Muhammad ibn Himyar."
"2350","2347 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Ukkashi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda reporting from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you writes to a person, let him begin with his name, and when he writes let him sprinkle dust upon his letter, for it is more successful."
"2351","2348 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs al-Awsabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Friday prayer, fasts that day, visits a sick person, attends a funeral, and attends a marriage, Paradise becomes due for him. No one narrated this hadith from Hariz except Muhammad ibn Himyar."
"2352","2349 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies guarding the frontier in the path of Allah, Allah will secure him from the trial of the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan except Muhammad ibn Himyar."
"2353","2350 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Ayyar, from Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his uncle Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever frightens a believer unjustly, it is incumbent upon Allah not to grant him security from the terrors of the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah except Muhammad."
"2354","2351 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be men from my nation who eat varieties of food, drink varieties of drink, wear varieties of clothes, and speak affectatiously; those are the worst of my nation. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr except Muhammad ibn Himyar."
"2355","2352 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Umm al-Darda who said: I asked Aishah: What would you provision him with when you traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), performing Hajj or campaigning with him? She said: I would provision him with a bottle of oil, a comb, a mirror, scissors, a kohl container, and a siwak."
"2356","2353 - And from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, who said: I heard Umm al-Darda narrating from Abu al-Darda who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: Do not get angry and Paradise is yours."
"2357","2354 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a chief, and the chief of the sitting place is facing the qiblah."
"2358","2355 - And with the same chain the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who raises his head before the imam and lowers it is not secure from Allah transforming his head into the head of a donkey. No one narrated these two hadiths from Muhammad ibn Khalid except Amr ibn Uthman."
"2359","2356 - Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shibami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the nearest then the nearest."
"2360","2357 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he did not consider stipulation in Hajj to be anything, and he would say: The Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) suffices you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mamar."
"2361","2358 - Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Raja al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hungers or is in need and conceals it from people and discloses it to Allah Almighty, it is incumbent upon Allah Almighty to open for him a good provision from lawful means. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Musa; Ismail is alone in transmitting it."
"2362","2359 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli informed us, he said: Abu al-Dahma al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will gather creation in a single plain, then He will raise for every people the gods they used to worship, and they will lead them to the Fire, while the monotheists remain. It will be said to them: What are you waiting for? They will say: We await a Lord we used to worship unseen. It will be said to them: Do you know Him? They will say: If He wills He will make Himself known to us. Then He, blessed and exalted, will manifest Himself to them, and they will fall prostrate to Him. It will be said to them: O people of monotheism, raise your heads, for Allah has made Paradise obligatory for you, and has placed in the Fire a Jew or a Christian in the place of every man among you. No one narrated this hadith from Umar except Thabit, nor from Thabit except Abu al-Dahma; al-Nufayli is alone in transmitting it."
"2363","2360 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn al-Rayyan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar al-Madani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the waiting period of Barirah that of a divorced woman."
"2364","2361 - And from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray while feeling anything in his stomach. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Mashar except Muhammad ibn Bakkar."
"2365","2362 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yaqub, from Abu al-Nadr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one night in Ramadan while people were praying, and said: Let none of you raise his voice over another, for that harms the one praying. No one narrated this hadith from Salim Abu al-Nadr except Muhammad ibn Yaqub; Anbasah is alone in transmitting it."
"2366","2363 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from his father, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The generous is near to Allah, far from the Fire, near to Paradise, near to people; and the miser is far from Allah, far from Paradise, far from people, near to the Fire. An ignorant generous person is more beloved to Allah Almighty than a worshipping miser. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya, from Muhammad, from his father, from Aishah except Said ibn Muhammad."
"2367","2364 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar, judge of Aleppo, narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prescribed prayer seated upon the ground, and sat in glorification upon the ground gesturing with gestures. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mukhtar except Hafs; Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"2368","2365 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Abu Rafi, that he gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glad tidings of the Islam of al-Abbas, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rafi except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it."
"2369","2366 - And from Shurahbil ibn Sad who said: I caught a bird among Banu Harithah, and Rafi ibn Khadij took it from me and released it, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared sacred what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah. No one narrated this hadith from Shurahbil except Abu Mashar."
"2370","2367 - Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I said to my father: O father, who is the man who rescued you from the polytheists on the day they beat you? He said: That was al-As ibn Wail al-Sahmi. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Hammad ibn Zayd; Sulayman ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"2371","2368 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad Ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Farwah Muslim ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Kab ibn Ujrah met me and said: Shall I not give you a gift? I said: Yes, give it to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we invoke blessings upon you, O People of the House? For we have learned how to greet you. He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Farwah except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, nor did anyone narrate it from Abd Allah ibn Isa except Abu Farwah."
"2372","2369 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer, and he said: Two by two. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin except Abu Asim."
"2373","2370 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perdition to gold and silver, saying it three times. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, what wealth shall we take? He said: A remembering tongue, a grateful heart, and a believing wife. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Murrah except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani al-Wasiti and Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad."
"2374","2371 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil and Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both said: Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he preached on Friday, would say: When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"2375","2372 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid al-Hunai narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: She is not lawful for the first until the other tastes her little honey. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Dinar is alone in transmitting it."
"2376","2373 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Hajib ibn Umar informed us, from al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, from Imran ibn al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: Those who do not seek ruqyah, do not cauterize, do not take omens, and trust in their Lord. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam ibn al-Araj except Abu Khushaynah Hajib ibn Umar."
"2377","2374 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Ashajj, the Ashajj of Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Bishr."
"2378","2375 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Jafar ibn Mahmud ibn Maslamah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Maslamah al-Ansari informed me, from Sad ibn Zayd ibn Sad al-Ashhali who said: A sword from Najran was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when it was brought to him he gave it to Muhammad ibn Maslamah and said: Strive with this in the path of Allah, but when the necks of people differ, strike it against a stone, then enter your house and be a discarded mat until a mistaken hand kills you or a decreed death comes to you. This hadith is not narrated from Sad ibn Zayd except with this chain; al-Hajabi is alone in transmitting it."
"2379","2376 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas - raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: Had you not sinned, Allah would have brought a people who sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness, and He would forgive them. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Yahya ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"2380","2377 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl informed me that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aish, beware of belittled sins, for they have a seeker from Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Said is alone in transmitting it."
"2381","2378 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, who said: Umm Jundub narrated to me that she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of the Jamrah, saying: O people, let none of you kill one another, and throw pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mufaddal except Hammad."
"2382","2379 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Suwayd ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, imam of the mosque of Quba, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Sulami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the abode of Banu Amr ibn Awf on Wednesday and saw a fortress in the properties and lands which he had not seen before, and said to them: O company of Ansar. They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers as ransom for you. He said: If only, when you descend for your festival, meaning Friday, you would remain until you hear my words from me. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers as ransom for you. When Friday came they attended the Friday prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he finished and prayed two voluntary rakahs at his station, though before that when he prayed Friday he would leave for his house and pray them in his house, until that day when he prayed them voluntarily in the mosque. When he finished he faced them, and the Ansar followed him from the mosque until they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: O company of Ansar. They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, with our fathers and mothers as ransom for you. He said: In pre-Islamic times, when Allah was not worshipped, you would bear the burden of the destitute in your wealth, do good, and join kinship; then when Allah favored you with Islam and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, you fortify yourselves. In what the son of Adam eats there is reward, in what birds eat there is reward, and in what beasts eat there is reward. The people left, and none remained except that he breached two or three gaps in his property, meaning he demolished in the walls of their orchards so the poor might enter and eat of the dates. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; al-Hajabi is alone in transmitting it."
"2383","2380 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: By your life, who said: By your life, O Muhammad."
"2384","2381 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Kab al-Azdi, the silk merchant, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Umm Salamah in Madinah with a veil between me and her, and I heard her saying: The most frequent supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. He said: There is no son of Adam except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; if He wills He leads it astray, and if He wills He guides it."
"2385","2382 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: Glory be to Allah, my Lord the Almighty, and with His praise, one hundred times, and likewise in the evening, no one of creation will come with the like of what he brought except one who said the like of what he said or more."
"2386","2383 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left my house except that he raised his gaze to the sky and said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from going astray or being led astray, slipping or being made to slip, wronging out of ignorance or being wronged in ignorance, wronging or being wronged. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah except Abu Bakr; Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"2387","2384 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad Ibn Aishah narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Imran; Ibn Aishah is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sad except with this chain."
"2388","2385 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman, then entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh and fulfilled his need with her, then came out and said: The woman approaches in the image of a devil and turns away in the image of a devil, so whoever finds that, let him go to his wife, for it repels what is in his soul. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Hisham; Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"2389","2386 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahr al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Bayan Abu Bishr, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes it will be said: O people of the gathering, lower your gazes; Fatimah bint Muhammad will pass. He said: So she will pass wearing two green garments. No one narrated this hadith from Bayan except Khalid; Abd al-Hamid and al-Abbas ibn Bakkar al-Dabbi are alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"2390","2387 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah who said: A man called Shihab was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Rather you are Hisham."
"2391","2388 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us, and we would bring him a basin of ours containing water; he would take a Madinan mudd, a mudd and a half or a third, and I would pour upon him: he would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth and sniff water, wash his face three times, his forearms three times each, wipe his head once, wipe his ears outward and inward, and purify his feet. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Yazid."
"2392","2389 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he wiped his head with leftover water in his hand, beginning from the back of his head, then drawing it to his nape, then drawing it back. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd Allah ibn Dawud."
"2393","2390 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Masruq al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is ablution, its prohibition is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Hassan; Abu Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"2394","2391 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri narrating from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah who said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe from a single vessel, which was the faraq. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim except Ibrahim."
"2395","2392 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to relieve himself beneath a fruit-bearing tree, and forbade relieving oneself upon the bank of a flowing river."
"2396","2393 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tale-bearing and listening to tale-bearing. No one narrated these hadiths from Maymun except Furat; al-Hakam is alone in transmitting them."
"2397","2394 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that a woman asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about purification from menstruation, and he said: Take your piece of cloth. She said: What shall I do with it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt shy, so Aishah said to her: Come to me and I will inform you: pass it over the outlet of the blood. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Hammad; Abu Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"2398","2395 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Hassan ibn Bilal, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and ran his fingers through his beard. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Sufyan is alone in transmitting it."
"2399","2396 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color the color of blood and the scent the scent of musk. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih."
"2400","2397 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek Allah's forgiveness seventy times a day."
